          "textEn": "8\nThese Shruti mantras state that every living being has a natural form, in which God\nexchanges a specific type of essence with. Only in a free state, this\noriginal essence can be fully experienced. In the physical world, the experience of rasa (aesthetic emotion) occurs in a distorted form,\nwhich is temporary. Thus, in the physical world, the display of rasa (aesthetic sentiment) occurs in the form of raudra (anger), etc. Therefore, the person who, having attained complete knowledge of these various 'rasas' (essences) in the form of the fundamental elements of activities,\nis the one who can understand the diverse forms of the original 'rasas' reflected in the physical world. The scholar, the student, wants to experience the real rasa in its spiritual form. In the beginning, he wants to become one with God. Thus, the ignorant spiritualist, without knowing the various flavors,\nwithout realizing the oneness with the complete soul, cannot go above.\nIn this verse, it is definitely said that the spiritual essence which is enjoyed\neven in a liberated state, can be experienced in the literature of Shrimad Bhagwat,\nbecause it is the ripe fruit of Vedic knowledge. By listening to this divine literature with humility,\na person can attain the desired complete bliss. But a person must be very careful in this matter\nthat the listening to this message is done with the right intention. The Shrimad Bhagavatam has been completely\nobtained only from a suitable source. It is Narad Muni, who brought it from Vaikuntha Loka, who\ngave it to his disciple, Shri Vyasadeva. Shri Vyasadev gave this message to his son Shukdev\nGoswami, and then he gave it to Maharaj Parikshit just seven days before his death.\nSrila Shukadeva Goswami was a liberated soul from his birth. To the extent that he\nwas liberated in his mother's womb itself, and after birth, he did not have to receive any kind of spiritual education. At the time of birth, no person is skilled from a worldly perspective, nor from a spiritual\nperspective. But being a completely free soul, Shri Shukdev Goswami\ndid not have to follow any kind of development method for spiritual realization."
