          "textEn": "56\nThey always have to be disappointed. It applies to other fields as well; no one is serious about life's\nproblems. Even those who are desirous of becoming one with the ultimate truth,\n(Mumukshu) are ready to commit spiritual murder for the sake of sensual pleasure. ©. But the Bhagwat\nsays that man should not live for sensual pleasure. The satisfaction of the senses is only up to that point,\nup to the point where it is necessary for self-preservation, not for the satisfaction of the senses. Because the body\nis made up of senses, and these senses desire some kind of satisfaction, therefore, for the satisfaction of such senses,\nsome rules and regulations have been made. But the senses are not for uncontrolled enjoyment. For example, marriage, that is, the union of a woman and a man, is necessary for procreation, but this\nis not for sensual pleasure.\nIn the absence of voluntary restraint, one has to promote family planning,\nbut foolish people do not know that as soon as they start searching for the ultimate truth,\nfamily planning happens automatically. Those who seek the ultimate truth are never attracted to unnecessary sensory gratification, because they are fully engaged in the work of seeking the ultimate truth. Therefore, in every area of life, the search for the ultimate truth should be the ultimate goal. From this,\nman will be happy because he will be less engrossed in various kinds of sensual gratification. And that supreme\nWhat is truth, its explanation has been given further.\nThey say that the knower of the essence of that which is beyond knowledge is non-dual.\nIt is spoken of as Brahman, as the Supreme Soul, and as God. 11. Meaning of the word:\nThey say--they say; Tat--that; Tattvavidah--the learned; Tattvamu--the ultimate truth; Yat--that; Gnanam--knowledge;\nAdvayam--non-duality; Brahma iti--known by the name of Brahma; Paramatma iti--known by the name of Paramatma; Bhagavan--God;\nIti--known by the name of God; Balaa--