सुदेव की वास्तविक अनुभूति के लिए भी होते हैं । वासुदेव का अन्य नाम\nयज्ञ है और भगवद्गीता में यह स्पष्ट कहा गया है कि सारे यज्ञ तथा कर्म, यज्ञ या भगवान्‌ विष्णु",
          "textEn": "8\n\nMeaning of the word\nVasudeva--God; Para--the supreme goal; Vedas--authentic scriptures; Basudeva--God; Para--for worship;\nMakha--Yagya (sacrifice); Vasudeva--God; Para--the means to attain; Yoga--yogic equipment; Vasudeva--of God;\nPara--subordinate to them; Kriya--action; Vasudeva--God; Param--the supreme; Gyanam--knowledge; Vasudeva--God; Para--the supreme--\nExtrem; Motion-- The goal of life.\n\nIn authentic scriptures, the ultimate purpose of knowledge is the perfect Supreme Being, Lord Krishna. The purpose of performing a yajna is to please them. Yoga is for their self-realization. All desires\nKarma is ultimately rewarded by them. They are supreme knowledge and all difficult penances are for knowing them. To serve them with love is dharma. They are the ultimate goal of life.\nMeaning: These two verses are in support of the fact that Lord Krishna is the only God worthy of worship. The goal of Vedic literature is also this, that a relationship with God should be established, and\nour forgotten loving service should be revived. It is the essence of the Vedas. This\nprinciple is confirmed by God in the Bhagavad Gita in his own words as follows: The ultimate purpose of the Vedas is only to know them. All the authentic branches, by God, having incarnated in the form of the body of Srila Vyasadeva,\nare created to remind the fallen souls bound by material nature of Lord Sri Krishna. No god can liberate one from physical bondage. This is the decision of all Vedic texts. The non-exclusive, those who do not have knowledge of the personality of God,\ndo not consider the omnipotence of God to be less, because they also describe them as other ordinary\nliving beings.\nFor this reason, the non-dualists are able to get freedom from material bondage with great difficulty. They are able to take refuge in him only after practicing divine knowledge for many births. Some may argue that Vedic rituals centered around sacrifices are upheld. That's true. But all such yagnas are also for the actual experience of Vasudeva. Vasudeva's other name is\nYagya, and it is clearly stated in the Bhagavad Gita that all yagyas and karmas, yagya or Lord Vishnu"
