          "textEn": "86\nGod, by one of his complete parts, stays with the living beings and becomes a guide in their material pleasures\nand remains a witness to all their activities. Where souls indulge in material pleasures, God remains unaffected by the material environment and remains in his divine position. The scriptures say that there are two birds on a tree.* One of them is eating the fruit of a tree, and\nthe other is watching his activities. This witness is God, and the bird that eats the fruit is\nthe soul. The one who eats the fruit (the individual soul) has forgotten its true form and is badly busy in the desires-driven actions of the material\nworld, while God (the Supreme Soul) always remains complete with divine knowledge. This is the only difference between the Supreme Being and the bound soul. The bound soul remains subject to the laws of nature, while the Supreme Soul is the controller of material power.\n\"Tara, the supreme, the friend, the equal, the tree, the one who is praised.\n\nTheir other, the other, the sweet, the sour, the bitter, the unpalatable, the bitter-tasting. ( Gues Upanishad 3.2.2)\n\nFootnote ends here. (... delete while formating in quark)\nAs the one who is beyond the senses, is one among the senses,\nSo is the self-existent one among beings and beings. 32). Meaning of the word\nAs-- in the same way; He-- in the same way; Avahitah-- associated with; Vahi-- fire; Darushu-- in wood; Ekah- one; Swa- in one's own womb; Yonishu- in one's own wombs;\nLike various beings; Vishch- soul- the Supreme Soul, God;\nIn beings, in living beings; Cha- and; Tatha- in the same way; Puman- supreme being..\n\nIn the form of the Supreme Being, God pervades all things in the same way as fire pervades within wood, and in this way, although they are one and unique, they appear in many ways.\nMeaning: The complete Supreme Personality of Godhead, Lord Vasudeva, expands throughout the entire material universe with his one quis,\nand His existence can 