          "textEn": "94\n\nMeaning of the word\nYasya-Whose; Avayavah-Of the body; Sansthanah-# Established; Kalpitah-Imagined; Lokah-Inhabited; Vistarah-Various; Tat-That; Vai-But that is; Bhagavatah-Of God; Rupam-Form; Vishuddham-Pure; Satvamu-\nExistence; Urjitam-Superior.\n\nIt is believed that all the universes are situated in the immense body of the Supreme Being\nBut they have no concern with the created physical organs. His body\nIs eternally spiritual and full of existence, which has no comparison. Meaning: The concept of the Supreme Being as the great-form or cosmic form is especially for those who are newly initiated, who are unable to think in terms of the divine form of God. For them, the meaning of form\nis any object associated with this physical world, therefore, in the beginning, to concentrate on the expansion of God's power,\nthe imaginative opposition of Brahman is necessary.\nAs said above,\nhas already happened, God expands his power in the form of the great element, in which all\nphysical elements remain included. In a way, the expansion of God's power and oneself,\nGod is one, but at the same time, the great element is also different from God. As a result, God's\npower and God are one and the same, different and non-different. Thus, the concept of the cosmic form,\nparticularly for the nirvisalitas, is inseparable from the eternal form of God. This form of God\nexists from before the creation of the eternal essence, and here emphasis is given\nthat the eternal form of God is supremely spiritual or divine from the qualities of nature. This\ndivine form of God manifests from the inner power, and in the form of many incarnations, their\nform remains with the same divine quality; there is not even a slight touch of greatness\nin it. Pashyantyado rupamadabhrachakshusha\nSahasrapadorubhojanaadhutam.\nSahasmurdhashravanaakshinasikam"
