          "textEn": "03\nMeaning: Lord Rishi Atri incarnated as Dattatreya, the son of Anasuya and Dattatreya. In the Brahmanda Purana, in the context of a devoted wife, the story of God incarnating as Dattatreya is described. In that, it is said that Rishi Atri's wife Anasuya prayed before Brahma, Vishnu,\nand Shiva, saying, \"O Lord! If you are pleased with me and ask me for a boon,\nthen my prayer is that you three together become my sons.\"They accepted this prayer.\nTowards this, God established self-realization in the form of Dattatreya and especially preached it to Alark, TER, Yadu,\nHaihay, etc. Then, the seventh, the auspicious sacrifice is performed.\nFrom these, the gods, the lords of the earth, and the self-existent ones. 12). Meaning of the word:\nThen-- After that; Saptame-- In the seventh; Saatvam-- Of Saatvam; Aakutiyam-- From Aakuti; Yagyah-- In the form of Yagya;\nAn avatar of God; Abhyajayat-- Became incarnated; Saah- These are the names; Yaam- From Yama etc.; Sur- Ganas-- Of the Ganas; Apaat- Ruled; Swayambhuva- Antaram- The time period of Swayambhuva Manu (Manvantara).\n\nThe seventh incarnation was Yagya, the son of Prajapati Ruchi and his wife Aakuti. He\ntook over the rule after the change of Swyambhuva Manu and received the help of gods like his son Yama. Meaning: To maintain the order of the physical world, the administrative positions accepted by the gods\nare given to highly virtuous beings.\nWhen such\npious souls are lacking, then God himself incarnates as Brahma, Prajapati, Indra, etc.,\nand takes over the responsibility of governance. In the time of Swayambhuva Manu (the modern era is of Vaivasvata Manu),\nthere was no suitable being who could take the position of Indra, the king of THAD. At that time,\nGod himself became Indra. Yama and others, with the help of their sons and gods, Lord Yagya\ntook over the rule of the world. In the eighth, Merudevyam, Urukrama was born from the navel."
