          "textEn": "5\nWe are pleased that people are taking interest in the non-violence movement of Lord Buddha. But will they take it seriously and completely shut down the slaughterhouses of animals? If that does not happen,\nthen the concept of non-violence has no meaning. The composition of Shrimad Bhagwat happened even before the beginning of Kali Yuga (five thousand years ago), and\nthe advent of Lord Buddha happened approximately two thousand six hundred years ago. Therefore, in the Shrimad Bhagavatam,\nthe prophecy of Lord Buddha has been given. It is an authentic scripture. There are many\nprophecies that are coming true one by one. All this will be indicative of the meaning of Shrimad Bhagwat, because it is free from any error, attachment, deceit, and incompleteness, which are the four faults of bound souls. The liberated souls are above these flaws, therefore they can predict the events of the distant future. Atthasau yugasanidhyam dasyuprayeshu rajasu.\nJanita Vishnu Yashasso Namna Kalkirjatpatih. 25. Meaning of the word:\nAtha--after that; Asau--that very God; Yuga-sandhyaam--in the twilight of the ages; Dasyu--a robber; Parayeshu--in comparison; Rajasu--\nA king; Janita--one who is born; Vishnu--one named Vishnu; Yashasah--one with fame; Naamna--by name; Kalki--\nAn incarnation of God; Jagat-patih--the lord of the world..\n\nThereafter, the all-powerful God will take birth in the twilight period of all two eras in the form of Kalki Avatar,\nand will be the son of Vishnu Yasha. At that time, the rulers of the earth will have become looters.\n\nMeaning: Here is another prophecy of God taking incarnation in the form of Kalki.\nHe has to be born in the twilight period of two eras, that is, at the end of Kali Yuga and at the beginning of Satya Yuga.\nSatya, Treta, Dwapar, and Kali, the cycle of these four eras continues like a month-cycle. The current\nKali Yuga will last for 432,000 years, out of which approximately 5,000 years have passed since the end