          "textEn": "29. They are externally related to this physical creation in the same way that someone consumes fragrance without being related to any\nfragrant substance. Therefore, without the support of God,\nthe essence, despite all efforts, does not reach God.\nNor does anyone, without skill,\nwithout skill, rise up in the womb. Namaani rupani manovachobhih\nSantanvato natcharyami vaagha. 37). Meaning of the word:\nNa- not; cha- also; asya- of the Lord; kashchit- any; nipunena- by skill; dhatuh- of the creator; avaiti- know; janta- living beings; kumaneeshah- ignorant; ootiha- of the works of God; namani- their names; rupani- their forms;\nManah- through speech; vachobhih- through words; santanvat- while expressing; nat- by acting; nat- by acting;\nIva- like; ajnah- foolish..\n\nFoolish men, due to their limited knowledge, cannot know the divine nature of God's forms, names, and actions, because they are acting like a character in a play.\nNor can such a person express such things through their logic or their speech.\nThey cannot. Meaning: no one can properly describe the divine nature of the supreme truth. Therefore,\nit is said that they are beyond the expression of mind and speech. Even then, there are some ignorant people\nwho, through their incomplete arguments and flawed descriptions of God's works, want to know the ultimate truth. For an ordinary person, the actions, manifestation, and disappearance of God,\nthe names, forms, equipment, personality, and all things related to them are mysterious.\n(Secret) are. There are two categories of materialists - one is the seekers of results, and the other is\nthe Mimansakas. The seekers of results have not even a little knowledge of the ultimate truth, and the Mimansakas,\nbeing disappointed with the results of their actions, turn their faces away from the ultimate truth, and through dry contemplation, they\ntry to know it. For all such people, the ultimate truth remains mysterious in the same way,"
