          "textEn": "[3]\nOne does not have to gain any personal benefit from exclusive devotion to God. They, without hesitation,\nserve God exclusively. In this creation, every creature is directly or indirectly serving God. No one is exempt from this rule of nature. Those who are being bound by the misleading\nrepresentatives of God and are indirectly serving God, they serve God in an adverse\nway. But those who directly serve under the direction of their beloved representative, they\nserve them favorably. Such favorable servants are devotees of God, and by the grace of God,\nthey are able to enter the secret realm of spirituality. But the mind's ideals always remain in darkness. As it is said in the Bhagavad Gita, God himself leads the pure devotees to the path of realization of the cause of their continuous loving devotion.\nThis is the secret to entering the abode of God.\nThere is no merit of deeds and no arguments for entrance there. There, the blessed Lord, thus.\nWhen the Sun God, the lord of all the worlds,\nThey perform the all-encompassing self-existence.\nWhere there is no repeated change, fierce. 39. Meaning of the word:\nAth--in this way; Iha--in this world; Dhanyaah--successful; Bhagvantah--known completely; Ittham-Esa; Yat-that;\nVasudeva--towards God; Akhil-complete; Loka-Naathe--towards the lord of all the universes; Karvanti-inspired;\nSarva-atmakam-100 percent; Atma-soul; Bhavam-aahad; Na-never; Yatra-where; Bhuyah-again;\nParivarah-repeated; Ugrah-terrible. In this world, only through such curiosities can a person be successful and fully known,\nbecause from such curiosities, divine\ngratitude and love towards the Lord, the master of all universes, arises, and a 100% guarantee of protection\nfrom the terrible repetition of birth and death is obtained.\nMeaning: Here, the praise of the curiosities of Shaunaka and other sages by Sut Goswami is based on their\ndivine nature. As has been said before, only devotees of the Lord"
