          "textEn": "87\nAre capable and by doing noble deeds (punya), one attains the world of ancestors. For the enjoyment of the senses, there are various arrangements in this life or in the next life after death. Some\npeople are trying to reach the moon or other worlds through the arrangement of machines,\nbecause they are eager to reach these worlds without doing any good deeds. But that is not going to happen.\nNo, hey. According to the laws of God, different kinds of beings can attain different realms of life only according to the deeds they have done. As it is said in the scriptures, only\nthrough good deeds can a person be born in a good family and attain wealth, excellent education, and\na good form. We also see that even in this birth, only through good deeds\ndoes a person receive good education or wealth. Similarly, we attain desired positions in the next birth only through good deeds.\nOtherwise, it would not happen that two people at the same time and in the same place are born and attain different positions. It is because of past karma. But all such\nphysical positions are temporary. Even in the highest Brahmaloka and the lowest Patala, these positions of ours\nkeep changing according to our actions. A person with a philosophical inclination should not be tempted by such changing\npositions. He should try to attain a permanent life of bliss and knowledge,\nso that he does not have to return again to this painful material world or any other realm. Sorrow and mixed happiness are two characteristics of this material life, and both are found in Brahmaloka and\nother worlds as well. These are also found in the lives of gods, and in the lives of pigs and boars.\nIn the sufferings and pleasures of all living beings, there is a difference in qualities and quantities, but\nthere is no one who is free from birth, death, old age, and disease. Similarly, everyone's happiness is also fixed.\nNo matter how hard anyone tries, some people will always get more or less of certain items. If they do come, they will come again. Therefore, a person should not waste time in these useless things,\nHe should only try to go back to God.\nShould be. This should be the goal of everyone’s life."
