दढता\nसे पालन करने वाले का; च- तथा \\",
          "textEn": "202\n\nMeaning of the word:\nIdhatham--in this way; Sharath--autumn season; Pravrushikau--yearly season; Ritu--two seasons; Harah--of God; Vishunvatah--of the wind;\nWhile constantly listening; Me--I myself; Anusavam--constantly; Yashah Amalam--white fame; Sankirtyamanam--going after chanting;\nBy the sages; Maha-atmadhih--by the great souls; Bhakti--devotional service; Pravritta--started flowing;\nSelf-life; Tol:--Rajoguna; Tam--Tamoguna; Upaha--destroyer..\n\nIn this way, in both the rainy and autumn seasons, I had the opportunity to continuously listen to the continuous chanting of the white glory of Lord Hari from these great sages. As soon as the flow of my devotion\nbegan, all the coverings of Rajoguna and Tamoguna were dispelled. Meaning: The divinely-willed service of God’s worship is the natural tendency of every being.\nThis\ntendency remains dormant in every being, but due to contact with the material nature, the Rajoguna\nand Tamoguna have been covering it since eternity. If a being becomes so fortunate by the grace of God and his great devotees\nthat he attains the company of pure devotees,\nand gets the opportunity to listen to the pure glory of God, then surely the flow of devotion\nstarts to flow like the flow of a river. Just as the river keeps flowing until it reaches the sea, Similarly, pure devotion flows with the company of pure devotees.\nThe stream continues to flow until it reaches the ultimate goal, that is, the divine love of God.\nIt does not reach.\nThe flow of devotion does not stop, but it increases unlimitedly.\nThe flow of devotion is so capable that even a spectator is freed from the influence of Rajoguna\nand Tamoguna. In this way, these two qualities of nature are removed.\nAnd the soul, attaining its original state, becomes liberated. To him who is attached, to him who is devoted, to him who is killed,\nTo him who is a treasurer, to the child, to the follower. 29). Meaning of the word:\nTasya--his/her; Evam--i