          "textEn": "203\n\nI was extremely attached to those sages. My conduct was humble, and because of their service,\nall my sins were destroyed. In my heart, I had a strong faith in them, off I\nhad subdued the senses, and I was following them with body and mind.\nI was following them. Meaning: For a person who desires to be elevated to the position of a pure devotee, these are the essential qualifications. Such a person should always seek the company of pure devotees. He should not be misled by a false\ndevotee. He himself should be simple and humble to receive teachings from a pure devotee. A pure devotee is one who is completely surrendered to the Lord. He knows God\nas the supreme master and others as his servants. Only by the association of pure devotees,\none can be freed from all the accumulated sins by worldly association. A newly initiated devotee\nshould serve the pure devotee with devotion. He should be extremely obedient and\nshould firmly follow the teachings.\nThese are the characteristics of that devotee who is determined to achieve success in this very life. Knowledge is the most secret, which is revealed by the self-realized.\nHe spoke, and they went away, kindly, with humility. 30>. Shabdartham (Meaning of the word)\nGyanam (Knowledge) - Gyan; Guhayatamam (Secret) - Guhayah; Yat - Which is; Tat - That; Sakshat - Directly; Bhagwata Uditam - By the Lord Bhagwan; Pratipadit - Proclaimed; Anvavochant - Given; Gamishyantah - While going; Kripya - Out of kindness; Deen-vatsalah - Those who are poor\nare very kind to. Extremely compassionate towards the humble people, those devotees of Vedanta, while leaving, gave me the teaching of that most secret subject,\nthe teaching of which is given by God himself. Meaning: The pure Vedanti or Bhakti Vedanti gives teachings to his followers according to the teachings of God himself. God has definitely given in the Bhagavad Gita and in all other branches\nThis teaching has been given that people should follow 