          "textEn": "205\n\nFrom that secret knowledge, I was able to precisely understand the influence of the power of Shri Krishna, who is the creator, sustainer, and destroyer of all substances. Upon knowing him, any\nhuman can return to him and meet him directly. Meaning: Any human being, through devotional service or through the knowledge of TRAE, can easily know\nhow the various powers of God work. From a part of the power,\nthe manifestation of the physical world happens, from the other (higher) part, the spiritual world (Vaikuntha) manifests\nhappens. These two powers manifest the intermediate beings, who serve one of the aforementioned powers. Living beings engaged in the service of physical power, for their existence and happiness,\nfiercely struggle, which appear before them as delusion (illusion). But those who\nlive in spiritual power, are given direct service to God in eternal life, complete knowledge, and uninterrupted bliss.\nAs the Lord has said in the Bhagavad Gita, it is His will that\nall the bound souls, who are rotting in the power of material energy, all the activities of this material world\ngive up and come back to Him. This is the most profound aspect of knowledge. But only a pure devotee\ncan understand it, therefore only they are able to reach the abode of God, to have a vision of him, and to serve him.\nFor that, they are able to reach. Its burning example is Narad Ji himself, who attained this state of eternal knowledge and eternal bliss. All its means and paths remain open for everyone,\nprovided that he agrees to follow the footprints of Shri Narad Muni. According to Shruti,\nthe powers of God are (naturally) infinite, and as has been said above, they\nare described in three main categories. This is indicated by Brahman, which is treated as the cause of the universe.\nIf the Lord, the Divine, is considered as the cause of action and the object of knowledge. 32)."
