          "textEn": "206\n\nMeaning of the word\nThis--so much; Sanshitam-- determined by scholars: Brahman-- this Brahmin Vyas; Tapa-Traya-- three types of suffering (pains);\nChikitsitam-- treated, medicine; Yat-- that; Ishva-Parimanakari-- supreme regulator; Bhagwati-- in God; Karma-- prescribed duty;\nBrahmani-- in Brahman; Bhavitam-- dedicated;\n\nOh Brahmin Vyasadeva, it has been determined by scholars that the best way to treat all sufferings and pains\nis to dedicate all your actions to the service of Lord (Shri Krishna)\nand surrender them. Meaning: Shri Narad Muni himself experienced that to open the path to salvation or to get rid of all the sufferings of life, the easiest and most practical way is to listen to the divine plays of God from the right and\nauthentic source with humility. This is\nthe only medicine for treatment. This whole physical world is full of suffering.\nFoolish people,\nOn the strength of their petty minds, in relation to the body and mind, and in the context of other beings,\nhave discovered many remedies to alleviate three types of suffering related to natural disasters.\nZ| The whole world is struggling hard to overcome these sufferings, but people do not know\nthat without God's permission, neither can peace nor relief be brought about by any plan or any method.\nIf God does not approve, then through medicinal treatment,\nthe effort to cure the patient will be in vain. If God does not approve, then crossing a river or sea by boat is not a cure. We should definitely know that\nGod is the ultimate giver of acceptance, therefore, for ultimate success or for the path of success,\nto get rid of obstacles, we should dedicate all our efforts to God. God is omnipresent, omnipotent, and omniscient. They are the ultimate approvers of all good or bad fruits.\nTherefore, we should dedicate all our actions to the grace of God.\nAnd accept them as the formless, transcendental, omnipresent, and supreme being, or the complete Supreme Personality of Godhead.\nWhether we are who we are, we should dedicate every object to the service of God. If there is any\nscholar, scientist, philosopher, poet, etc., then he should establish the supremacy of God"
