          "textEn": "207\nFor that, use your knowledge. Try to study the power of God in every sphere of life. Do not boycott them, nor try to become equal to them by collecting little knowledge, or to take their place. If there is any administrator, politician, warrior,\netc., then he should try to establish the supremacy of God in Rajdharma. He wants to fight for God, just like Arjun. In the beginning, the great warrior Shri Arjun\nrefused to fight, but when God assured him that fighting\nis necessary, he changed his mind and fought for God. Similarly,\nIf there is any businessman, industrialist, or farmer, then he should spend his hard-earned money\nfor God. One should always think that whatever accumulated wealth there is, it is God's\nwealth. Sampada is regarded as the goddess of fortune (Lakshmi) and Lord Taur Narayan or\nLakshmipati.\nTherefore, try to engage Lakshmi in the service of Lord Narayana and become happy.\nBecome. This is the way to experience God in every sphere of life. Ultimately, the best\nthing would be to get rid of all physical activities and dedicate oneself to listening to the divine\nleelas of God. But if such an opportunity is not available, one should try to\ndevote oneself to the service of God towards whatever things one is attracted to. This is the path to peace and prosperity. In this verse, the word 'sanchitam' is also important. No one\nshould ever think that Narada's experience was merely childish imagination. It isn't. This feeling has been experienced by skilled and eminent scholars, and this is the real meaning of the word 'Sansuchitam'. The one who is the cause of the creation of all beings, by whom good conduct is established,\nThat very wealth does not diminish by being treated. 33)."
