          "textEn": "20\nA deep interest in listening to the divine plays of God will be generated, which will allow him to attain the natural state of gross\nand subtle bodies, and even beyond that, with the pure soul and the Supreme Soul,\nhe will be able to gain knowledge of his eternal relationship. After joining the establishment of eternal relationship,\ngradually, pure devotion to God develops and takes the form of complete knowledge of God,\nwhich is beyond the periphery of the attributeless Brahman and the indwelling Supreme Soul. From such a supreme yoga,\nwhich is mentioned in the Bhagavad Gita, a man becomes complete in this very body, and in that supreme\nmagnitude, the best qualities of God begin to appear. Such gradual development happens with the company of pure devotees.\nWherever action is performed, it is for the sustenance of the divine.\nKnowledge is subordinate to that, which is united with devotion. 35). Meaning of the word\nYat--Whatever; Atra s--In this world; Jivan--In life; Jagat--In the world; Kriyate--Is done; Karma--Work; Bhagavat--Of God; Paritoshnam--For satisfaction; Gyanam--Knowledge; Yat-That--That which is said in this way; Adheenam--Dependent; Hi--Indeed; Bhakti-Yoga--Devotion\nRelated; Samanvitam--Combined; Bhakti-Yoga--Devotion\nRelated; Samanvitam--Combined; Bhakti-Yoga--Devotion\nRelated; Samanvitam--Combined; Bhakti-Yoga--Devotion In this life, whatever work is done for the satisfaction of God, that is called Bhakti Yoga.\nOr, what is called divine love and devotion towards God, and what is called knowledge, that becomes a co-factor. Meaning: Generally, the popular belief is that by performing actions with desire, following the prescribed method of scriptures,\na person becomes capable of attaining divine knowledge for self-realization. Some people\nconsider Bhakti Yoga as the second form of Karma. But in reality, Bhakti Yoga is above both Karma and knowledge. Bhakti Yoga is independent of knowledge or action, while knowledge and action are dependent on Bhakti Yoga.\nThis is Kriyayoga or Karma Yoga, which Narad has praised for Vyas, has been specially praised,\nbecause the main principle is to please God. God does not want his sons\nto be afflicted by the three types of suffering of life. They keep wanting that they all are with them"
