          "textEn": "228\n\nWhen all apprehensions and personal errors are removed, then there is ideal faith in the divine element,\nand interest in it increases in greater proportion. Attraction arises from this state,\nand after this, the state of emotion is attained, which is the previous state of unwavering love towards God. These states are all different stages of the development of divine love. In this way, divine\nbeing overwhelmed by love, there is a strong feeling of separation (separation), which leads to the origin of eight types of\ndifferent emotions. The shedding of tears from the eyes of the devotee is its natural reaction,\nand since Shri Narad Muni had attained this state immediately after leaving his home in his previous birth,\ntherefore, it was easy for him to see the presence of God, which he had easily experienced without\nany physical impurity through his developed spiritual senses.\nOverflowing with love, filled with joy, and filled with delight.\nIn the blissful abundance, both of them are seen by the sage. 17. Meaning of the word:\nLove--love; excessive--excessive; different--differently distinguished; feeling of elation; limbs--of the body;\nDifferent limbs; overflowing--being completely overwhelmed; joy--joy; in the ocean--in the sea; absorbed--engrossed; not--\nNot; to see--to see; both--both; sage--Oh Vyasadeva,\n\nOh Vyasadeva, at that time, due to the feeling of elation, every limb of my body\nwas thrilled. Because of being immersed in the ocean of bliss, I could see myself and God\nas well. Meaning: There can be no worldly comparison between happiness and intense joy, and spiritual experiences.\nTherefore, it is extremely difficult to express such experiences. Such a glimpse of joy can be found in the words of Shri Narad Muni. Of the body or of the senses,\neach part has its own special function.\nUpon seeing God, all the sar\nWake up to serve God, because in a liberated state, the senses are of God"
