          "textEn": "307\nTatparya: The physical world is Gag, while the supreme abode is Ekarup. The dualistic world is made of matter\nand the soul, while the supreme world is entirely the soul, in which not even a trace of material qualities\nis found. In this selfish world, every person tries to become the master of a false world,\nwhile in the supreme world, God is supremely important, and all others are His unique servants.\nare. In this complex world, every person is jealous of everyone else, and because of the duality of matter and soul, death is inevitable. For the surrendered soul, God alone is the only refuge. Without taking refuge in the lotus feet of God, no one in this material world can save themselves from the cruel claws of death. Abhidravati mamish sharastaptayaso vibho.\nMay the work be accomplished, O Lord, may I not be ruined in my womb. 10. Meaning of the word\nAbhidravati--Oh, now it happened; Mam--My; Ish--Oh Lord; Sharah--Arrow; Tapt--Like fire; Ayasah--Iron; Vibho Hey\nGreat; Kamam--Desire; Dahatu--Let it burn; Mamu--To me; Nath--Oh Protector; Ma--My; Mat--My; Me--My womb;\nMay there be no miscarriage..\n\nOh Lord, you are almighty. A scorching iron arrow is coming towards me rapidly.\nis coming. My Lord, if it is your will, let it burn me, but do not burn my womb\nand cause abortion. Oh Lord, please have so much grace on me.\n\nMeaning: This incident is after the death of Uttara's husband, Abhimanyu. Abhimanyu, a widow,\nUttara, following her husband, but she was pregnant and a great devotee of God,\nMaharaj Parikshit was in her womb, therefore, protecting him is her supreme duty.\nA mother has a great responsibility to protect her child in every way, therefore, God,\nUttara was not ashamed to speak her mind before Shri Krishna.\nUttara, the daughter of a great king, a\nGreat brave wife and a great devotee, a disciple of the king. Later, she also became a great queen.\nShe was fortunate in every way."
