          "textEn": "308\n\nSoot said:\nUpadharya Vachastasya, the Lord is devoted to his devotees.\nTo accomplish this unrighteous act, Drona's heart was filled with anger. 11. Meaning of the word:\nSuta said - Suta Goswami said; Upadharya - Listen carefully; Vachah - Word; Tasyaah - His; Bhagavan - God;\nBhakta-vatsalah - One who is very loving towards his devotees; Apandavam - Without the descendant of Pandavas; Idam - This;\nKartum - To do this; Dronaah - Son of Dronacharya; Astram - Weapon; Abudhyat - Understood..\n\nSoot Goswami said: Hearing his words with patience, towards his devotees,\nLord Shri Krishna immediately understood that Dronacharya's son\nAshwatthama has released the Brahmastra only to destroy the last descendant of the Pandava dynasty. Meaning: Even though God is impartial in every way, He still favors His devotees, because\nIt is absolutely necessary for the well-being of every individual.\nThe Pandava-clan was a devotee-clan,\nTherefore, God wanted them to rule over the world. This was the reason that Duryodhana's army\nended the rule and established the rule of Maharaja Yudhishthira. Therefore, they were trying to protect Maharaj Parikshit, who was in the womb. They did not want the world to be devoid of the Pandava clan, which was the ideal family of devotees. Jeane, the best of the wise, the five-fold, the wise.\nTurning towards the self, the luminous, the innumerable, the gems are offered. 12). Meaning of the word:\nTarhi-then; Eva-also; Ath-therefore; Muni-great sage; Pandava-the sons of Pandu; Pancha-five;\nSayakan-weapons; Atmanah-self; Abhimukhan-towards; Diptaan-lamped; Aalakshya-by seeing; Astraani-weapons;\nUpadudu-accepted. Hey, the leader among the great thinkers (Shaunaka Ji), seeing that blazing Brahmastra\ncoming towards him, the five Pandavas took up their respective five weapons."
