          "textEn": "32\n\nMeaning of the word:\nMa-- opinion; Manasthaah-- think; Hi- certainly; Etat- this all; Aashcharyam- astonishing; Sarva- all; Aashcharyamaye- by the astonishing;\nExtremely astonishing; Achyute- without; Yah- who; Idam- this (creation); Mayaya- by their power; Devya- divine;\nSrijati- creates; Avati- sustains; Hanti- destroys; Ajah- unborn..\n\nOh Brahmins, do not think that this is particularly astonishing in the activities of the secret and unbroken Lord. They, with their divine power, wisely nurture, protect, and destroy all material things, although they themselves are unborn. Meaning: For the joy of living beings, the activities of God are always unimaginable.\nFor God, nothing is impossible, but all his actions seem astonishing to us,\nand thus he always remains beyond the limits of our intellect. God.\nThe Almighty and the Perfect God.\nGod is 100% complete, while in the other sense, Narayan,\nBrahma, Shiva, the gods, and all other living beings, only a percentage of such completeness is found. No one is equal to him, nor is anyone greater than him. They are unique. With the self-controlled, freed from external light, with Krishna.\nFacing the departure, Krishna, this is what Pritha said. 17). Shabdartham\nBrahma-tejah - Radiation of Brahmastra; Vinirmuktayah - free from obstacles; Atmajih - his sons; Saha- together; Krishnaya- to Krishna; Prayan- going; Abhimukham- facing; Krishnam- Lord Krishna; Idam- this; Aah- said; Pritha- Kunti;\nSati- a devotee of God, Sati..\n\nIn this way, escaping from the radiation of the Brahmastra, the devotee of God, Sati Kunti, addressed Shri Krishna in this way, as she was about to depart for her home with her five\nsons and Draupadi. Meaning: Kunti is said to have been a Sati here out of unconditional devotion to Lord Krishna. Now his heart will be expressed in the praise of God given ahead.\nA true devotee of God never asks for mercy from any living being or deity,\neven to alleviate the suffering o