          "textEn": "370\n\nWith that, along with the great fortunes, the best of wealth. Worshipped by the knowers of dharma, the knower of space and time. 9>. Meaning of the word:\nTan-un all; Sameetan-- together; Maha-bhagan-- extremely powerful men; Upalabhya-- having obtained; Vasu-uttamah--\nThe best among the Vasus (Bhishma Deva); Pujayam-- welcomed; Dharma-gyah-- knower of Dharma; Desh-sthan-- place and time; Kaal-- time;\nVibhag-vit-- one who adapts himself according to country and time.\n\nThe best among the eight Vasus, Bhishma Deva welcomed all the great and powerful sages gathered there, because Bhishma Deva had a thorough knowledge of all religious\nrules according to country and time. Meaning: The learned know very well how religious principles should be harmonized according to time and place. All the great teachers or religious preachers or reformers of the world,\nby harmonizing religious rules according to time and place, fulfilled their purpose.\nIn different parts of the world, there are different types of climate and conditions, and if someone\nhas to preach the message of God, then he should be able to reconcile things according to the country and time.\nShould be. Bhishmadev was one of the twelve great men who preached this Bhakti Sampradaya,\nTherefore, he could welcome and honor the powerful sages who came from every corner of the universe while lying on his deathbed. Undoubtedly, at that time, he himself was unable to welcome and honor them by getting up, because at that time he was neither at home nor in a normal state\nHe was in a healthy condition. But they were very agile from their brain working smoothly.\nAnd they spoke soft and gentle words. That is why all the guests were properly welcomed. A human can fulfill his duty through mind, speech, and action. They knew very well that\nhow they should be used in the appropriate place.\nTherefore, even though physically incapable,\nhe had no difficulty in receiving the honor of the people.\nKrishna, who is aware of his power, is seated as the Lord of the Universe."
