          "textEn": "374\n\nIn my opinion, all this has happened because of the strong time, by being subjected to which everyone\nevery person wanders around in every world, just as clouds are carried from here to there by the wind. Meaning: Within this universe, in all the space, the control of time is in the same way, as\nin all the worlds, its control is. All the big planets, including the sun, are controlled by the force of the wind,\njust as clouds are carried from here to there by the speed of the wind. Similarly, it is also the controller of the action of the inevitable time, air, and other elements.\nTherefore, every object is ultimately controlled by time, which is the most powerful representative of God within this physical world. Therefore, Yudhishthira should not be saddened by the unimaginable events of this era.\nShould not be.\nAs long as a human being lives in these physical world conditions, until then he has to\nendure the actions and reactions of time. Yudhishthira should not think that\nhe had committed a sin in his previous life, the result of which he is having to suffer. Even the greatest\npious person has to suffer the conditions of material nature. But the virtuous one is devoted to God,\nbecause he is guided by an honest Brahmin and a virtuous Vaishnava. These three guiding principles should be the goal of life. Man should not be distracted by the ways of eternal time. Even Brahmaji, the great controller of the universe,\nis subject to time. Therefore, even though he is the true custodian of religious principles, man\nshould not be disturbed by being controlled by time.\nWhere the son of Dharma, the king, wielded the mace, the mighty-armed one.\nKrishna, the axe, and the bow, were friends, then disaster struck. 15). Shabdartham\nYatra--where; Dharma--righteousness; Suta--son; Dharmaraja's son; Raja--king; Gada-Panih--one who holds a powerful mace in his hand;\nVrikodara--Bhima; FT:—Arjuna; Astri--one who wields a weapon; Gandivam--the Gand