          "textEn": "385\nPhysical life is produced only because of the natural desires of the living being. By devotional service to God,\nthe natural desires of the soul are not killed, but rather they are put into the right work of devotional service. This brings the ability to be transferred into the Vaikuntha of desires. Here,\nSenapati Bhishmadev is mentioning a special type of yoga, which is called Bhakti Yoga.\nAnd he was fortunate that before abandoning the physical body, he was seeing God himself\npresent before him. Therefore, in the next verses, he has expressed his wish that God remains before his sight.\nSadevadevo Bhagavantam Pratikshatam\nKalevaram Yavadidam Hinomyaham.\nAdorned, with beautiful, tusk-like eyes, joyful,\nWith lotus-like face, four-armed. 24). Meaning of the word:\nSah-He; Dev-Devah-Gods of the Gods, the best of lords; Bhagavan-Lord; Pratikshitam- Please wait;\nKalevaram-To the body; Yavat-Until; Idam-This; Hinomi-I sacrifice; Aham-I am; Prasanna-Delighted; Haas-Laughing;\nArun-Lochan-Red eyes like the morning sun; Ullasat-Adorned with beautiful clothes; Mukha-Ambhuja---Like a lotus,\nHis face is like that; in the path of my meditation; four-armed: -Narayana (worshiped by Bhishpadeva) with four arms;\n= Four-armed form, like the rising sun, with lotus-like eyes and beautifully adorned, smiling;\nMy Lord with lotus face, please wait here for that moment until I leave my\nThis physical body. Note: Bhishmadeva knew very well that Lord Krishna etc. are Narayana. Their\nsacred deity was the four-armed Narayana, but they knew that these four-armed Narayana are a complete part of Lord Krishna.\nIndirectly, he expressed his wish that Lord Shri Krishna should appear in his four-armed Narayan form. A Vaishnava is always humble in his conduct. Although it was 100%\ncertain that Bhishmadev was going to Vaikunthaloka even after leaving this body, still, in the form of a humble Vaishnava,\nhe wanted to see the beautiful face of God, because he thought that somewhere this"
