          "textEn": "400\nGoing to retire; all--all; senses of senses; activity--activity; delusion--being attached; Tuva--He\nPrayed; Janayamu--material shelter; Visrijan--renouncing; Janardanamu--to the controller of living beings..\n\nWhile seeing Lord Shri Krishna through pure meditation, he immediately became free from all material inauspicious\nstates and from the physical pain caused by the arrows. In this way,\ntheir functions of all senses stopped, and they, while abandoning the body, praised the divine controller of all\nliving beings. Meaning: This physical body is the gift of that physical energy which is called Maya. Due to forgetting his eternal relationship with God, man begins to consider the physical body as his own form.\nFor a pure devotee of God like Bhishmadev, this illusion disappears as soon as God arrives. Lord Krishna is like the sun and the illusory external material power is like darkness.\nIn the presence of the sun, it is not possible for darkness to persist. Therefore, as soon as Lord Krishna arrived, all the material impurities were completely removed, and Bhishmadev, along with the substance, became able to attain the divine position by stopping the functions of the impure senses. The soul is fundamentally pure.\nAnd that is why the senses are also pure. It is from the impurity of the physical body that the senses start working with incompleteness and\nimpurity. But as soon as one is in contact with the supremely pure Lord Krishna, the senses\nare freed again from material impurities. Before Bhishmadeva gave up his body, he was able to attain such a divine state only because of the presence of God. God is the controller of all beings.\nHe is benevolent. This is the decision of all the Vedas. They are the supreme eternal and the supreme among all eternal beings * and they are the ones who fulfill all the needs of all kinds of beings ©.\nIn this way, they provided all the facilities to fulfill the divine wishes of their supreme devotee,