          "textEn": "406\nTherefore, piercing the body of Lord Krishna with arrows by Bhishma Deva is a delusive problem for the non-devotees and atheists,\nbut those who are devotees or liberated souls are not deluded.\nBhishma Deva praised the all-compassionate posture of the Lord, because he did not leave Arjuna\nalone, although he was distracted by Bhishma Deva's arrows. Neither did they have any hesitation in coming near Bhishma's deathbed, although Bhishma had mistreated them on the battlefield. In this state, both Bhishma's repentance and the Lord's compassionate smile are unique. The great Acharya and devotee of the sweet essence of God, Shri Vishwanath Chakravarti Thakur, has said a very important thing in this\nrelation. They say that the sharp arrows of Bhishmadev, from the wounds that arose in the body of the Lord,\nwere appearing to him in the same way as a pincushion of a lover in the body of the Lord.\nBeing slapped by a lover in this way, even if it causes a wound in the body, is not considered a symbol of enmity. Therefore, the war that took place between God and his devotee, Shri\nBhishmadev, was an exchange of divine bliss. It was not in any way\nworldly. In addition to this, since God's body and God are inseparable, therefore, the supremely complete\nThere was no possibility of wounds in the body. Wounds caused by sharp arrows are\nscorching to the common person, but the one who has even a little supreme knowledge will understand it as a divine exchange of valor. The Lord was very pleased with the wounds caused by Bhishma's sharp arrows. The word 'vidhyaman'\nis extremely important, because God's skin is not different from God. Because our skin\nis different from our soul, therefore, for us, the word 'vibhidyasan' or 'rubbed' and 'cut'\nwill be very appropriate.\nDivine bliss is of many kinds, and in this world, all the\nactivities that are there, they are merely reflections of divine bliss. Because every object in this world\nis worldly, therefore it is full of madness, but in the supreme world, every object is of the same supreme\nnature, therefore there are various kinds of enjoyments without madness. God to his supreme"
