          "textEn": "429\n\nChapter ten\n\nThe departure of Lord Krishna for Dwarka.\nShaunaka said,\nHaving killed the angry and agitated, Yudhishthira, the best among the righteous,\nWith his associates, having eaten, how did he proceed? What did he do then? 1>. Meaning:\nShounak said -- Shounak asked; Hatva-- after killing; Swariktha-- legitimate ancestral property; Spruhda-- desire to snatch; Se-- from; Atatayinah-- aggressors; Yudhishthira-- King Yudhishthira; Dharma Bhrutam-- those who follow Dharma; Vrishtah– the most; Saha-anujaih– with his younger brothers; Pratyavruddha– stopped; Bhojanah– accepting the necessities;\nKatham kase? Pravritta– engaged; Kim– what; Akarit– accomplished; Tat– thereafter; Tatpashchit– after that.:\n\nShaunaka Muni asked: Those who wanted to seize the legitimate ancestral property of Maharaj Yudhishthira,\nhow did the greatest virtuous Yudhishthira, after killing those enemies, govern his subjects with the help of his brothers? Certainly, they could not enjoy their empire\nfreely, but from infinite consciousness.\nMeaning: Maharaj Yudhishthira was the best among all righteous people. Therefore, they were not ready to enjoy the empire,\nto fight with their cousins, they were not ready for the right purpose,\nfight, because the kingdom of Hastinapur was their legitimate ancestral property and their cousin wanted to\nseize it. Therefore, they fought under the guidance of Lord Krishna for the right purpose,\nBut they could not enjoy the fruits of their victory, because all their cousins were killed in the war.\nThey were gone. Therefore, he ruled the empire, but considering it his duty and with the help of his younger brothers,\nhe ruled. Shaunaka Rishi's curiosity was important; he wanted to know\nwhat his behavior was like when Maharaj Yudhishthira got the opportunity to enjoy the empire."
