          "textEn": "449\n\nAt the end of one hundred years of age (according to our calculation, 8,64,00,00,000 X 30 X\n12 X 100 solar years), the entire universe is completely destroyed, and both times, the co-existence\nThat is, physical power and the element of life, that is, the element of the base, merge into the body of God. All beings remain dormant in the body of God until the second creation of the world\ndoes not happen. This is the law of creation, preservation, and destruction of the physical world. When moved by God, the physical creation happens through the interaction of the three qualities of material nature, that is why it is said here that before the three qualities of material nature were moved,\nGod was present. In the Shruti mantra, it is said that before creation, there was only the supreme Lord Vishnu.\nAt that time, there was neither Brahma, nor Shiva, nor any other deity. Vishnu means\nMahavishnu, who is lying in the Karantaranav sea.\nFrom their breath, all the universes are produced in seed form,\nand slowly, within each universe, the immense form of countless planets develops. The seeds of the universe take on a huge size in the same way that countless banyan trees develop from the seeds of a banyan tree. These are the complete parts of Lord Mahavishnu, Shri Krishna, as mentioned in the Brahma Samhita as follows--\n\n^“ I respectfully bow to that original Lord Govinda, whose complete part is Mahavishnu. The leaders of the universes, all the Brahmas, after the universes born from the pores of their divine body, live only as long as God exhales.\" (Brahma Samhita 5.58)\n\nThus, Govinda, that is, Lord Krishna, is also the cause of Mahavishnu. Women must have heard this\nVedic truth from some authentic source, that is why they were talking about it.\nThe only way to gain accurate knowledge of divine subjects is through an authentic i | There is no alternative to it."
