          "textEn": "273\n\nWhatever has been said above, while all that is happening, God continues the business of creation, and while doing so, He grants salvation to those enemies of His own whom He has killed. They are supreme.\nThey are also attractive to the liberated soul, therefore they are worshiped by all the gods, like the great Brahma and Shiva. Even in his male avatar, he is the master of creation. The material\nCreation is kept functional under his supervision, as testified in the Bhagavad Gita (9.10). They\nare like Kunji, the controller of physical power, and in countless universes, they are the root cause of countless incarnations for the control of physical power. In other universes, in addition to other incarnations,\nin only one universe, there are more than five hundred thousand incarnations of Manu.\nBut in the spiritual world,\nbeyond the great element, there is no question of incarnations--but in various Vaikuntha realms,\nthere are complete parts of God. In Vaikuntha, there are planets three times the number of planets found within the countless universes of the great element. And all the Narayana forms of God are parts of his Vasudeva-\nform. In this way, they are together Vasudeva, Narayana and Krishna. They are Shri Krishna, Govinda, Hari.\nMurareh, O Lord, Narayana, Vasudeva are--all in one. Therefore, no matter how great someone may be, God\ncannot calculate the qualities.\nI bow to the self, and to the best of the gods, to the gods, to the sages, and to all the classes and castes. 31st. Meaning of the word:\nAtmanam--self; cha--also; anushochami--I am grieving; bhavantam--you; cha--also; amar-uttamam--the best among the gods;\nDevan--for the gods; pitran--for the inhabitants of the pitra world; rishin--for the sages; sadhun--for the devotees;\nSarvan--all; varan--for the castes; tatha--and; ashraman--for the four ashrams of human society..\n\nHe is the best among the gods, I am thinking about myself and about you, and along with that,