          "textEn": "292\n\nDharma said,\nThis is the word of the Pandavas, fearless of death. By the virtues of the Yashas, Krishna, by the service, God has created. 17). Meaning of the word:\nDharma: Thus spoke Dharma; Etat-all these; Vah-by you; Pandavayanam-of the Pandava dynasty; Yuktam- fitted; Upayuktam- fitted; Aarti- one who suffers; Abhayam- freedom from fear; Vachah-word; Yesham-by them; Gunagainai- by their qualities;\nKrishna- Krishna also; Dautya-first-first; Dautya-first; Karmai-by deed; Kritah-done; Sampanna-completed; Krishna-Krishna; Dautya-first; Dautya-first; Krishna-Krishna; Dautya-first; Krishna-Krishna; Dautya-first; Krishna-Krishna; Dautya-first; Krishna-Krishna; Dautya-first; Krishna-Krishna; Dautya-first; Krishna.\n\nDharma said: The words you just spoke are entirely appropriate for a Pandava-descended person. Lord Krishna, impressed by the devotion of the Pandavas, fulfilled the messenger's duty. Meaning: The assurances and promises given by Maharaj Parikshit were not exaggerations of his true power. The Maharaja had said that those who violate religion, even if they are residents of heaven,\nstill cannot escape their strict rule.\nThey were not only proud of falsehood, because a devotee of God\nis like God himself, and sometimes, by his grace, becomes even more powerful than him, and if\na devotee makes a promise, even if it seems difficult to be fulfilled in general, but by the grace of God,\nit is fulfilled properly. The Pandavas were able to become the charioteer of God or sometimes the messenger of God through their unique devotion and complete\nsurrender to God. For the devotees,\nsuch works done by God are greatly pleasing to them, because God wants to serve those unique devotees\nwho have no other work besides serving God with love. The famous friend and servant of God, Arjuna's grandson, Maharaj Parikshit, was pure, just like his grandfather.\nHe was a devotee. Therefore, God was always with them--even when they were in the mother's womb and they were\nattacked by Ashwatthama's burning Brahmakha, even then they were with them.\nThe devotee always remains in the protection of God,\ntherefore, the assurance of protection given by Maharaj Parikshit could not be meaningless. Dharma accepted this fact and thanked the king for giving assurance in accordance with his high prestige."
