ं के\nपरम कारण हैं । ब्रह्म - सहिता में भी इसकी पुष्टि हुई है कि भगवान्‌ कृष्ण ही समस्त कारणों के अन्तिम\nकारण हैं |",
          "textEn": "294\n\nKechid vikalpavasana aahu ratmanamatmanah. God is beyond destiny, karma is beyond nature, and the Lord is beyond all. 19. Shabdartham\nKeetcham--any one of them; Option-Vasanaah--denying all kinds of duality; Aahuhu--declare; Atmanam--oneself; Atmanah--oneself; Daivam--divine; Anye--others; Apara--other; Karma Karma;\nSwabhavam--nature; Apara--other, many; Prabhum--Lord; Swi. Some philosophers who deny all kinds of dualism declare that man\nis responsible for his own happiness and sorrow. Other people say that divine powers are responsible for this,\nwhile there are also some people who say that karma is responsible for this,\nand those who are completely materialistic believe that nature is the ultimate cause of this.\nMeaning: As has been said above, philosophers like Gemini and their followers establish\nthat desire-driven actions are the root cause of all happiness and sorrow, and if there is any superior authority, any\nsuperhuman, powerful God or deity, then they too are subject to the influence of desire-driven actions, because they\ngive results according to the actions of the people. He says that karma is not independent, because karma is accomplished by some\ndoer, therefore the doer is the cause of his own happiness or sorrow. In Bhagavad Gita (6.5)\nit is also confirmed that through a mind free from material attachment, man can liberate himself from the sufferings of the world. Therefore, one should not put oneself in bondage due to the physical attachment of the mind.\nShould not. In this way, the human mind itself is his friend or enemy in his happiness and sorrow.\nAtheists, materialists, and skeptics conclude that physical nature is the cause of all causes.\nAccording to them, the combination of physical elements is the cause of physical happiness and sorrow, and the disintegration of matter is the cause of being freed from all physical heat. Gautam and Kanada consider the combination of atoms\nto be the cause of every object, and Ashtavakra, like an atheist, finds that the spiritual light of Brahma\nis the cause of all causes. But in the Bhagavad Gita, God himself declares\nthat He is the formless Brahma & Khot. Therefore, they, that is, the personality of God, are the supreme cause of all causes. It is also confirmed in the Brahma-Sahita that Lord Krishna is the ultimate cause of all causes."
