          "textEn": "300\nThe so-called progress is the root of all unrighteousness, and that is why adultery, bribery, and nepotism are prevalent.\nHmm. Man cannot stop these evils by laws and police, but he can cure the disease of the mind by\ntaking the right medicine. This medicine is to be a supporter of the rules of Brahmin culture, that is, penance, purity, compassion, and truth. Modern civilization and economic development are creating a new situation of poverty and scarcity.\nDue to this, consumer goods are being black-marketed. If in society, leaders and\nwealthy individuals spend half of their accumulated wealth on these misguided people and give them divine\nconsciousness, that is, the knowledge of Bhagavat, then surely Kali Yuga will fail to trap these bound souls in its net.\nWe should constantly remember that false ego, high estimation of our life's values, excessive attachment to the senses, or their association and intoxication will lead to human\ncivilization from the path of peace, even if people make a lot of noise for world peace,\ndo not do. The teaching of the principles of Bhagwat will make all human beings self-controlled, clean from inside and out, compassionate towards the suffering,\nand truthful in their daily conduct. The evils of human society, which are clearly visible in today's time,\nThis is the only way to fix them.\nNow, the path of righteousness is to follow the truth.\nThat which is unrighteous, is driven away by unrighteousness, and is destroyed by Kali. 25. Meaning of the word:\nIdayam--At this time; Dharma--This Dharmarupa; Pada--Feet; Te--Yours; Satyam--Truth; Nirvartayet--To live in some way; Yatah--From which; Tam--That; Jighrukshati--Attempting to destroy; Adharma--Inferior form; Ayam--This; Anruten--By deceit, untruth\nFrom; Etadhitah--Increasing; Kali--Sakshat Kali (kalah) +\nNow you are standing on only one foot, which is your truth, and you are now somehow\nliving. But this discord-like form, which blooms and flourishes through deceit, also wants to destroy that foot. Meaning: The rules of religion are not based on any customs or human-made formulas, but on four basic practices--\nTapas (penance), cleanliness, compassion, and truth. The common people should be taught to practice these principles from childhood. The meaning of penance is to willingly accept such things, even if"
