          "textEn": "33\nBy doing, and (5) by staying in a place with an environment filled with divine consciousness. If the state is operated by the aforementioned method, then naturally there will be divine consciousness everywhere. All kinds of gambling (dice), even betting, lead to downfall, and when\ngambling is encouraged in the state, then the truth is completely lost. From the aforementioned age,\nfor a longer period, young men and women should be allowed to remain unmarried, and all kinds of\nbutcher shops should be prohibited from having licenses. Non-vegetarians should consume meat only through a government-approved method, otherwise not. All kinds of intoxication, even smoking cigarettes, chewing tobacco, and\ndrinking tea should also be prohibited.\nAgain, for the sake of asking, the Lord gave the form.\nThen, the untrue, my desires, the passion, the animosity, and the five. 39. Meaning of the word:\nAgain - then; Cha - also; Yachamanaya - to the beggar; Jata-rupam - gold; Adaat - given; Prabhuh - the king; Tatah - from that;\nAnrutam - untruth; Madam - intoxication; Kamam - lust; Rajah - due to the quality of passion; Vairam - enmity; Cha - and so; Panchamam -\nWhen Kali asked for something, the king granted him permission to live in that place\nWhere gold is available, because wherever there is gold, there lies untruth, intoxication, lust, envy\nand animosity. Meaning: Although Maharaja Parikshit allowed Kali to live in four places,\nit was difficult to find such places in his kingdom, because during the reign of Maharaja Parikshit,\nthere were no such places anywhere. Therefore, Kali pleaded with the king to give something that\nwould be practical and useful for his deceitful acts.\nIn this way, Maharaj Parikshit gave him permission to live in that\nplace where gold resides, because where there is gold, the aforementioned four\nobjects are found; in addition to that, animosity (vair) also remains. In this way, the Kali gold-\nbecame standardized. According to Shrimad Bhagwat, gold encourages false speech, intoxicating substances, prostitution,\njealousy and enmity. Even gold-standard exchange and currency are bad."
