          "textEn": "326\n\nMeaning of the word\nUnderlined-- Almost everything has been described; Etat-- These all; Vah-- To you; Punyam-- Holy; Parishitam-- About Parikshit; Maya-- By me; Vasudeva-- Of Lord Krishna; Katha-- Stories; Upetam-- In the context of; Akhyanam--\nNarration; Yat-- Which; Aprachhat-- You asked me..\n\nOh sages, as you asked me, now I have narrated almost all the stories related to Lord Krishna's history of the holy King Parikshit.\n\nMeaning: Srimad Bhagavat is the history of the activities of God. And the activities of God\nare completed only with the devotees of God. Therefore, the history of devotees is not different from the history of the activities of Lord Krishna. The devotee of God understands the activities of God and his pure devotees\nas the same, because they are all divine. Yayyaah Kathaa Bhagavathaan Kathiyorukkarman.\nThe male organs are the instruments of action, the female organs are the senses. 10>. Meaning of the word:\nYaha Yaha-- who who; Kathaah-- stories; Bhagavatah-- about God; Kathaniya-- to tell me off; Uru-karmanah-- wonderful deeds; Ashrayah- enshrined; Pumbhinah-- by humans; Sansveyah- to be heard\nshould be; Taha- all those; Bubhushubhih- by those who desire their own welfare\nShould be; Taah- those; Shravan Chadahiye.\nMeaning: By regularly listening to the divine activities, virtues, and names of Lord Krishna,\na person progresses towards eternal life. Regularly listening means to gradually\nknow them correctly and in their true form, and knowing them in this way means to attain\neternal life, which is mentioned in the Bhagavad Gita. Such divine glorious activities of Lord Krishna\nare medicines prescribed to cure birth, death, old age, and disease, Those who consider life as material\nAwards. Thus, the accomplished state of life, the culmination, is the goal of human life, and\nThe attainment of divine bliss is."
