          "textEn": "352\nHe serves, but it does not mean that he will eat and drink only in the master's plate. This\nThe mentality of false prestige is the reason for the complete collapse of the social system, and we can see\nthat its origin was done by an experiential-zero Brahmin boy. Just as dogs are not allowed to enter rooms and\nstoves and hearths, even if the master has kept a dog, similarly, according to Shringi,\nthe king had no right to enter the house of Shamik Rishi. From the child's opinion,\nthe king himself was at fault, not his own father, and in this way, he justified his peaceful father\nto be fair. Krishna Gate Bhagavati Shastaryutpathagaminam.\nI am the one who is the cause of the origin of the Tadit, I am the one who sees my strength. 35). Meaning of the word:\nKrishna--of Lord Krishna; Gate--after departing from this world; Bhagwati--God; Shastari--the supreme ruler; Utyatha--\nGaminam--to the travelers; Tat Bhed - by being separated; Sethun Rakshakah - the protector; Adai- today; Aham--I; Shasmi--I will punish;\nParyat--to see; Me--mine; Balam--valor.\n\nAfter the departure of Lord Shri Krishna, the supreme ruler, our protectors have left,\nBut these miscreants are flourishing. Therefore, I will take this matter into my own hands and punish them. Now look at my prowess. Meaning: That inexperienced Brahmin, proud with little divine power, was captivated by the magic of Kali Yuga. Maharaj Parikshit had given permission for Kaliyuga to live in four places, as it has been said before, but under the very efficient rule of the king, Kali could not find a place to live anywhere in these designated places.\nHe could not find a place.\nTherefore, Kaliyuga was in the process of showing its power, and by the grace of God, it\nIn this proud, inexperienced Brahmin boy form, it found a hole. This small Brahmin, for destruction,\nwanted to show his power, and he showed the audacity to punish a great king like Maharaj Parikshit. He wanted to take his place