          "textEn": "374\n\nBy the teachings of pilgrimage,\nthey themselves re-establish the pilgrimages. 8. Shabdartham\nTatra varaha; upajagamuha - pancha; bhuvanam - the universe; pujanaha - those who worship; mahaa-anubhavaaha - great-bodied;\nMunayaha - the sages:--Thinkers; disciples --with their disciples; mostly ~ often; pilgrimage pilgrimage place; approach --journey; advice --for the sake of;\nWith the excuse of; themselves -self; certainly -certainly; pilgrimages -all places from pilgrimage; sanctify -make holy; saints -mendicants \\,\n\nOn that occasion, great intellectuals, along with their disciples and their presence,\nBy the means of pilgrimage, the sages who certainly sanctify the pilgrimage places arrived there. Meaning: When Maharaj Parikshit sat on the banks of the Ganges, this news spread in the universe in all four\ndirections, and the very intelligent sages, who could understand the importance of this occasion,\ncame there, pretending to be on a pilgrimage.\nIn reality, they had come to meet Maharaj Parikshit,\nThey had not come to take a bath, because they were capable of sanctifying all the pilgrimages. Common people\ngo to pilgrimage sites to wash away all their sins. In this way, pilgrimage sites become burdened by the sins of others. But when such sages travel to burdened pilgrimage sites, they purify those places with their\npresence. Therefore, the sage who came to meet Parikshit,\ndid not care to purify himself like ordinary people, but he came to meet Maharaj Parikshit in that place\nunder the pretext of bathing, because he had predicted\nthat Shukdev Goswami would deliver a discourse on Shrimad Bhagwat. They all wanted to take advantage of this great occasion.\nAtri, Vasishta, Chyavana, Sharadva,\nNarishtanemi, Bhrigu, and others.\nParashara, Gadhisuta, and Rama,\nUttathya, Indra, Pramade, and the wind. 9>. Medhatithirdeva Arthisheno\nBhardwaja Gautamah Pippalada\nMaitreya Oravah Kavashah Kumbhayoni-"
