          "textEn": "2\nAlways remained cheerful, therefore, when Maharaj Parikshit was about to die, to help in the method of self-realization,\nShukdev Goswami was sent to provide assistance. Maharaj Parikshit, from his childhood,\nwas a devotee of Lord Krishna, therefore he had a natural affection for Krishna. Shukdev Goswami knew this devotion,\nTherefore, he welcomed questions about the duties of the king. Because the king had indicated that the ultimate duty of every living being is to serve Lord Krishna, therefore Shukdev\nGoswami, welcoming this suggestion, said, \"Since you have asked questions about Krishna, therefore\nyour question is very glorious.\"\" The first verse is translated as follows.\nShri-Shuka said:\nThose who ask questions: What is the benefit of the world to the king?\nHe who is self-controlled, is praised by men, and is superior to others. 1>. Meaning of the word\nShri-Shukah Uvacha--Shri Shukadeva Goswami said; Variyan--Very; Eshah--This; Tete--Yours; Prashna--Question, question;\nFe: Done by you; Lok-hitam-- Beneficial to all human beings; Nrip--Oh King; Atmavit-- Spiritualist,\nYogi; Sammitah-- Accepted; Punasam-- Of all men; Shrotavya-Adishu-- In all kinds of hearing; Yah-Who is; Parah-Supreme,\n“ Shukadeva Goswami said: Oh King, your question is glorious, because it is very beneficial to all\ntypes of people. The main subject of listening to the answer to this question is\nand all the spiritualists have accepted it. Meaning: This question itself is so excellent that it is the best topic of hearing (listening). By merely asking and listening to such a question, a person can attain the highest state of life.\nBecause\nLord Krishna is the supreme being, therefore any question about him is original and complete. God\nShri Chaitanya Mahaprabhu has said that the ultimate perfection of life is to attain the divine love devotion of Krishna. Because the questions and answers about Krishna are the ones that grant a divine status to man, therefore, regarding the vision of Krishna,\nthe questions of Maharaj Parikshit are extremely glorious. Maharaj Parikshit wanted to completely immerse his mind in Krishna,\nand this is possible only by listening to the extraordinary activities of Krishna. For example, the Bhagavad Gita says that Krishna's manifestation, disappearance, and his pastimes"
