hould not become a karmi, that is, he should not become a beneficiary of the fruits of his own good or bad deeds.\nShould not want. He should not do any good or bad deed for himself, but every thing should be done for the sake of the supreme\nLord God. This method of action is also mentioned in the Bhagavad Gita (9.27)"
