          "textEn": "5. Therefore, whoever follows the footprints of the ideal reader or ideal listener, Shukdev Goswami and Maharaj,\nUndoubtedly, he will attain salvation just like them. Maharaj,\nParikshit attained salvation only through hearing, and Shukdev Goswami attained salvation only by preaching. Discourse (text) and listening are two of the nine devotional activities, and by partially or wholly following these principles, a person can attain the supreme position. Therefore, the complete lesson of Shrimad Bhagavat, starting from the first verse of Janmadyasya and ending with the last verse of the twelfth canto, Maharaj,\nwas narrated by Shukdev Goswami for the attainment of salvation by Parikshit. It is mentioned in Padra Puran\nthat Gautam Muni advised Maharaj Ambarisha to regularly listen to the Parayan of Shrimad Bhagwat by Shukdev Goswami.\nHere is its confirmation that Maharaj Ambarisha listened to Shridbhagavat from beginning to end in the same form in which Shukdev Goswami preached it. Therefore, one who\nhas an interest in Bhagwat should not, by reading some parts from here and some parts from there,\nplay around with it, but he should follow the footsteps of great kings like Maharaj Ambarisha or Maharaj Parikshit, and listen to it only from an authentic representative of Shukdev Goswami. Etachnirvidyamananimichatamakutobhayam |\n\nYoginam nrip nirnitam harinamanukotanam | 11>. Meaning of the word\nThis is; Nirvidyamananam-- those who are completely free from all material desires, theirs; Ichchatam-- those who are desirous of all kinds of\nmaterial pleasures, theirs; Akutham-- fear; free from all doubts and fears; Yoginam-- of the satisfied; Nrip-He\nKing; Ninnitam- Certain truth; Hare-of Lord Krishna; Naam-holy name; Anu-behind someone, always; Kirtanam-\n॥ Rajan, following the great men, constantly chanting the holy name of God is the undoubtedly and fearless path to success for all those\nwho are free from all material desires, or who are desirous of all material pleasures, and also for those who are\nself-satisfied due to divine knowledge. Meaning: In the previous verse, the utterance of the immense need for devotion to Mukunda was made"
