          "textEn": "8\nHe keeps sinning, thinking that by chanting the holy name of God, the effects of sins will continue to be nullified, then he\nis the biggest offender at the feet of the holy name. Such criminals, by any proposed method of purification,\ncannot purify themselves. In other words, even if someone is a sinner before chanting the holy name of God,\nonce they take refuge in the holy name of God and become protected,\na person should abstain from sin with the hope that this holy name-chanting will protect them. The eighth offense is to consider the holy name of God and its method of chanting as equivalent to any material auspicious deed. There are many types of auspicious deeds for material gain, but the holy name and its\nchanting are not only holy auspicious service. Undoubtedly, the holy name is a holy service, but its use should not be done for such\npurposes. Because the holy name and God are one and the same power, therefore the holy\nname should not be dragged into the service of humanity. The sentiment is that God is the ultimate enjoyer.\nHe is neither\na servant of anyone, nor is he obedient. Similarly, since the holy name of God is distinct from God,\ntherefore, the holy name should not be used for personal service. The ninth offense is to preach to such people about the divine nature of the holy name, who do not want to chant the holy name of God.\n\nIf such a sermon is given to unwilling listeners, then\nthis act is considered a sin at the feet of the holy name. The tenth offense is to show aversion towards the holy name of God even after hearing about the divine nature of the sacred name. The effect that is experienced by chanting the holy name of God is the liberation of the worshiper from the concept of false ego. False ego manifests because of considering oneself the enjoyer of the world and thinking that all things in the world are for one's own use.\nThe entire materialistic world is under the control of the false ego of 'I' and 'mine',\nbut to be free from such a delusional belief is the real effect of chanting the holy name. That which is beyond the reach of many, is not considered good.\n\nThe auspicious moment is known, which is beneficial. 12)."
