          "textEn": "63\nIt is called repetition. We want to find a solution to all these problems of life, but we\ndo not know that path. Here is a suggestion that whoever wants to get rid of these vices of life--such as birth, death, old age--\nand the recurrence of disease, © should worship only God, not anyone else, as suggested in the Bhagavad Gita (18.65). If we truly want to end our\nbonded life, then we should worship Lord Krishna, who is in the heart of every living being due to his part-form\nnatural affection for all beings (Bhagavad Gita 18.61).\nIt is natural that a child in the lap of his mother remains attached to his mother, and the mother also remains\nattached to the child. But when the child grows up and becomes accustomed to circumstances, then he\ngradually becomes separated from his mother, although the mother keeps wanting the child to do some service.\nShe herself remains equally affectionate towards that child, but the child's nature of forgetting\nis there. Similarly, since we are part of God, God always remains affectionate towards us and wants\nto remain that we go back to His abode. But we are such bound souls that we do not care about them, and\nkeep running after delusive physical bonds. Therefore, we should break all the delusive bonds of the world\nand, by serving God, try to meet Him again, because He is the ultimate truth\n. In reality, we remain just as longing for them, just as a child remains longing for its mother. To seek God we do not have to go far, because He is present in our midst. But,\nIt does not mean that we should not go to places of worship, such as temples, churches, and mosques. Worship\nThese sacred places are also associated with God, because God is omnipresent. For the common person,\nthese sacred places are centers for learning divine science.\nWhen temples become devoid of rituals, then people's\ninterests do not remain in such places that the general public gradually becomes godless, and\na godless civilization arises. From such a hellish civilization, in the problems of life, artificially\nthere is an increase, and people's lives become difficult. Such fools of a godless civilization,\nUnder the patented trademark of materialism, to bring peace and prosperity in the godless world"
