          "textEn": "8l\nLives are based on false ego and these are expressed through his childish and futile activities\nas a desire to gain victory over the laws of nature and to assert dominance over the resources of the five elements. When such a mindset exists, a person becomes confident in the power of physical science, which includes the discovery of atomic energy and space travel by mechanical vehicles, and\nthrough such petty achievements of physical science, even the power of that egoistic God\nis challenged, which can end all these petty efforts of man in less than a moment. A well-established soul or a Brahma-Siddha soul understands very well that the Supreme Brahman or God is\nThe all-powerful Vasudeva, and that (the self-realized being) is a part of the supreme complete. In this way, his\nnatural state is to cooperate with God in the form of a divine relationship between the servant and the served.\nSuch a self-realized being ceases to display its futile activities of asserting dominance over material nature.\nIt stops doing it. Because of being well acquainted with the scientific method, he completely engages in the faithful devotion of God. A capable yogi who practices controlling the life force through the accepted method of yoga,\nis advised to give up the body in this way--He should press the anus with the heel of his foot,\nand then rotate the life force sequentially through all six places (chakras)--these places are--\nnabhi (navel), abdomen, heart, chest, palate, eyebrows, and TERT. Controlling the life force through the accepted yoga method\nis mechanical and this method is a kind of\nphysical effort for spiritual perfection (siddhi).\nIn ancient times, such practice was very common for a yogi, because\nin those days, the style of life and character was favorable off. But in the present time, when the influence of Kali Yuga\nhas become so disturbing, then almost every person in the art of this physical exercise\nis unskilled. In these days, by