          "textEn": "94\nHe--that (devotee); gross-and-subtle; senses--senses; the point of detachment--the point of indifference; mind--maya--\nmental level; divine-maya--in the quality of goodness; the action-maya--the action of ego; the state--by crossing over; by progress; with--together;\nby them; comes--goes; complete knowledge; truth--the essence; quality--the attribute; complete blockage--completely blocked\n\nIn this way, the devotee crosses over the gross and subtle coverings and enters the level of ego\n. In that state, he merges those physical qualities (Rajo and Tamo Gunas) into this indifferent point,\nand in this way, he attains a virtuous ego. After this, all ego\nmerges into the great essence, and he attains pure self-realization.\nMeaning: As we have stated many times, pure self-realization is the pure consciousness of accepting oneself as a constant servant of God. In this way, man is re-established in his original state of divine love and devotion to God, as clearly stated in the next verse. Without receiving any kind of remuneration from God, or in any other way, this state of loving devotion to God can only be attained when the physical senses are pure, and the original pure state of the senses is regained.\nTF | Here it is suggested that the senses can be purified through yoga--in this, the gross\nsenses become absorbed in the quality of Tamas, and the subtle senses in the quality of Rajas. The mind is related to the quality of goodness.\nTherefore, it is called divine. The complete purification of the mind is only possible when a person becomes a constant servant of God\nand becomes stable.\nTherefore, even the pure attainment of Sattva is a physical attribute; man has to\ntranscend this physical state of Sattva and reach the pure Sattva or Vasudeva Sattva. This\nVasudeva Sattva helps in admitting a human being into the divine abode. In this context, we must remember that compared to the above method, the method of gradual upliftment of devotees,\nalthough authentic, is not useful for the present era, because people are fundamentally unaware of yoga practice.\nEven if the so-called yoga practices by professional supporters are beneficial for physical activities,\nsuch a small success cannot be helpful in achieving the spiritual upliftment described here. Five thousand years ago, when the level of human society was completely according to the Vedic system, So, the yoga method described here was a common thing for every person, because every\nperson, especially Brahmins and Kshatriyas, staying away from home, in the Brahmacharya Ashram, under the protection of a guru"
