          "textEn": "55\nIt happens that when the divine stories of God are received by a person devoid of materiality from a devoted devotee,\nthey show an effect like an injection. In other words, when stories of Shrimad Bhagavat are heard by professional listeners,\nthey do not work in the miraculous way mentioned above. The devotional listening to the stories of God is not like listening to ordinary conversations,\ntherefore, its effect will only be felt by a devout listener when the gradual dispelling of ignorance\noccurs. Whose devotion to God is such that it is in God and also in the Guru. Those who are spoken of by him, how do they shine? (Shvetashvatara Upanishad 6.23)\nWhen a hungry person is given food, his hunger is satisfied, and along with that, the joy of eating is attained. In this way, there is no need to ask him whether\nhe has actually received food or not.\nThe fire test of listening to Shrimad Bhagwat is whether a man\nhas attained decisive light or not.\nWe will now examine this again through the illusion of the self. Here, He creates the unmanifest, the manifest, the Supreme Being. 6>. Meaning of the word\nBhuyah-- again; Ev-- also; Vivisami- I am eager to know; Bhagavan-- God; Atma-- private; Mayaya-- from the powers;\nYatha- in the way; Idam- this world; Srujate- creates; Vishcham- the universe; Durvibhavyam- inconceivable;\nAdhishwaih- by the great gods L\nI want to know from you how God creates these visible universes in this form\nwith his own personal powers, which are even more inconceivable than the greatest of gods. Meaning: In every curious mind, the important question of the creation of this visible world keeps arising.\nIs. Therefore, such a question by a person like Maharaj Parikshit is not unusual, because\nhe had to understand all the activities of God from his guru. We each unfamiliar object"
