          "textEn": "65\n\nTherefore, the conclusion is that a serious devotee should first go to such a guru who\nis not only proficient in Vedic literature but also a great devotee, who has a realization of God and His\ndifferent powers. Without the help of such a devotee-guru, no person can progress in the spiritual science of God. A trustworthy guru like Shukdev Goswami not only tells about the inner powers of God,\nbut also tells how they live with their external power. In the inner power, the pastimes of God are displayed as the activities of his Vrindavan,\nbut the activities of his outer power are manifested in the forms of his causal Vishnu, the nourisher of the womb, Vishnu, and\nthe nourisher of milk.\nSrila Vishwanath Chakravarti, while preaching to the Vaishnavas,\nsays that they should not only be interested in listening to the activities of God (Yatha Rasaleela),\nbut should also be interested in the creation element Leelas performed in the form of their incarnations,\njust as Maharaj Parikshit, as an ideal disciple, was off from the ideal Guru Shukadeva Goswami.\n\nSuta said,\nThus, the king was pleased to hear the praises of Hari. Hashikeshmanusmrty prativaktum pracarem. 11 Nl\nMeaning\n\nSuta said-- Suta Goswami said; Thus-- In this way; Upamannitah-- Upon being requested; Raja-- By the king; Guna-\nAnukathne- In the description of divine qualities; Hareh- Of the Lord; Hashikeshham- To the lord of the senses; Anusmritye- By remembering; Prativaktum- To give an answer; Prachamre- To complete the offerings.\n.\n\nSut Goswami said: When the king prayed to Shukdev Goswami in this way that he\ndescribe the creative power of God, then he remembered Indra's lord (Shri Krishna)\nproperly and spoke thus to give an appropriate answer. Meaning: When devotees of God have to give a lecture and describe the divine qualities of God,\nthey do not think that they can do anything independently. They think\nthat they can only do this when the lord of the senses, God, does not inspire them to speak. Jeev kau"
