          "textEn": "774\nYou are the one who gives, I know the truth, you are the one who loves me. Abandon all other faiths and surrender to me alone. I will liberate you from all sins, do not grieve. **My dear Arjun! You are very dear to me. Therefore, for your own welfare, I will reveal my most\nsecret teaching. It is like this - you become my pure devotee and give me self-surrender. I give you the promise of a complete spiritual life, by which you will be able to daily\nobtain the right to my divine love and devotion. You abandon all other religious practices and come to my only refuge.\nCome and believe that I will save you from all sinful deeds and redeem you.\nI will do. Do not worry even a little.\n\nThose who are intelligent pay attention to this final teaching of God. Spiritual realization TAH is the first step in that direction. The next step is the Isha-\nexperience, which is called deeper knowledge.\n'The ultimate culmination of the knowledge of the Bhagavad Gita is the realization of God.\nAnd when someone attains this state, they voluntarily become a devotee of God and start\ndevoting themselves to divine love. This devotion to God always depends on love for God, and\nthe service accepted in Karma Yoga, Gnana Yoga, or Dhyana Yoga is different from formal service. In the Bhagavad Gita, there are various teachings for different classes of\npeople, and various descriptions of Varnashram Dharma, Sanyas Dharma, Yati Dharma, the detached state of life,\nInner control, meditation, Yogic powers, Kaushi, Siddhi, etc., are found, but the person who,\nwith the intention of serving God, goes to their refuge with love and attachment, only he is able to assimilate the essence of the knowledge described in the Vedas. He who accepts this method with skill, he immediately\nAttains the perfection of life. This is what is called the life-achievement of Brahman.\nAs Srila Jeeva\nGoswami explained based on Vedic assurances, ​​Brahmagati means to attain a spiritual form like God, and in that form, the liberated soul constantly resides in one of the Vaikuntha realms.\nThis accomplishment of life is attained by the pure devotee of God without performing rigorous penance for accomplishment."
