          "textEn": "90\nThose who, at the beginning of creation, expanded the powerful knowledge in the heart of Brahma and gave the inspiration of complete knowledge about creation\nand about themselves, and those who appeared from the mouth of Brahma, may they be pleased with me. Meaning: We have already explained that from Brahma to the smallest ant, all living beings'\nIn the form of God, God provides desired knowledge to every living being. Every living being has the ability to acquire 78% of complete knowledge in the ratio of 50:64 from God. Because the soul is merely a natural part of God,\ntherefore, it is unable to assimilate the complete knowledge of God. In the state of bondage, the individual loses all memories of the body's changes or death. This knowledge again\nIn every living being, is inspired by God from within the heart of the living being, and this is what is called the awakening of knowledge,\nbecause it is equivalent to waking up from sleep or unconsciousness.\nThis awakening of knowledge is completely subordinate to God.\nTherefore, in the practical world, different types of knowledge are found in different individuals. This awakening of knowledge does not happen spontaneously, nor is it a physical interaction. Its fulfillment\nis the direct God (Dhiyan Patih), because even Brahma is subject to this rule of the supreme creator. In the beginning of creation, Brahma is born without parents, because there was no other creature at that time. Brahma\nis born from that lotus, which appears from the navel of Garbhodakshayi Vishnu, and that is why they are called Aja\n. These are Brahma or Aja, also living beings in the form of a part of God, but being the most pure devotees of God,\nafter God creates the main creation, he inspires them to create through nature. Therefore, neither nature nor the Supreme Being is independent of God.\nPhysicists can only observe the reactions of nature.\nThey do not understand the direction working behind such activities, which\nis like a child watching the electrical feats, but he has no\nknowledge of the engineer of the power plant. This incomplete knowledge of the physicist is due to his lack of comprehension. Therefore, Vedic\nknowledge was first introduced into the inner self of Brahma, which makes it seem that Brahma himself is the distributor of Vedic\nknowledge. Undoubtedly, Brahma is the exponent of Vedic knowledge, but in reality, God"
