          "textEn": "97\nYat--that; WAH--characteristics; Yat--that; Adhishthanam--background; Yat--that; Srishtam--created; Idam--this world; Prabhoh--Oh Lord;\nYat--in which; Sansthitam--established; Yat--that; Param- in control; Yat--that which is; Cha--and; Tatu--this; Tatvamu--characteristics;\nBad--Please describe; Tatvat--in reality; HL--\n\nOh Father, please describe the real characteristics of this expressed world. What is its basis? How did it originate? How is it structured? And all this, under whose control\nis being done? Meaning: Based on the real cause and action, the questions raised by Narad Muni seem extremely\nlogical. But atheists keep presenting many self-created theories in which\nthere is not even a trace of cause-and-effect. This expressed world and soul, even now, these godless atheists\nbased on experimental knowledge, are uninquired, although they have presented many theories created by their fertile minds.\nBut Narad Muni, contrary to such mental contemplative principles, was eager to know all the facts related to creation, not through those principles. In divine knowledge related to the soul and the Supreme Soul, the knowledge of the world and its creation's foundation\nis included. In the practical world, any intelligent person sees three things in reality:\nthe living being, the expressed world, and the ultimate control over them. An intelligent person can see that neither the living being,\nnor the behavioral world, are created by coincidence. Behind the creation and its regulating causes,\nthe planning of some intelligent mind seems to be working. Through pure curiosity and with the help of someone who truly knows them, the ultimate cause can be discovered.\nAll Pg Bhavan Veda Bhut-Bhavya-Bhavatprabhu:\nKaramlak-vad fas Vigyanavasitam Tava. 3). Meaning of the word\n\nSarvam- all aq; hi--certainly; etat--this; bhavanu--you; veda--know; bhuta--whatever is produced; bhavat-prabhuh--you, the master of all; kara-amalaka-vat--like a mango 