          "textEn": "200\nBesides their father Brahma, there is no other source of creation. Therefore, they wanted to know everything about Brahmaji,\nregarding their subject. He who is absorbed in the supreme austerity, O Lord. Then, do not think of yourself as beyond doubt.7/. Meaning of the word\n\nSah--He; Bhavan--You; Acharat--Did; Ghoram--Difficult; Yat Tapah--Meditation; Su-Samadhah--Complete discipline; Tena--That\nCause; Khedayase--Give pain; Nah--To us; Tvam--You; Para--The ultimate truth; Shankham-Doubt; Cha--And; Yachchasi--To us\nGiving opportunity EL\n\nEven then, when we think about the complete difficult penances performed by you while staying in complete discipline,\nwe are more amazed than you about the existence of any person\n, Although you are so powerful in the matter of creation.\n\nMeaning: Following the footprints of Shri Narad Muni, a man should not blindly consider the Guru as God.\nThe respect of a guru is considered equal to God, but\nwhoever calls himself God, should immediately abandon him. Narad Muni had accepted Brahma as God because of the wonderful work of creating\nthe universe, but when he saw that Brahmaji was also worshiping some superior\nman, he became suspicious. God is the greatest. He has no worshiper. The one who worships with the intention of becoming God himself is deluded, but\nan intelligent disciple can immediately recognize that God does not need to be worshipped by anyone, even\nhimself. Even if worshipping is a method for divine experience,\nhe can never become God through it. No person can become God through self-realization.\nThrough method. Narad Muni had thought of Brahmaji as the supreme being, but when he\nsaw that he was engaged in the method of divine experience, he became doubtful.\nTherefore, they wanted accurate information."
