          "textEn": "207.\nBeing deluded by the miraculous power of God, everyone considers God. A man like Brahmaji, who is accountable,\ndoes not like to be called God by his disciples or dependents, but foolish people, when praised by men like dogs,\npigs, camels, and horses, and when addressed as God,\nbecome extremely elated. Why do such people tremble when called God or called God by foolish admirers?\nThe explanation for this is given in the next verse. O deluded one, by whose sight I am lost,\nI am deluded, and I am wandering in vain. 13. Meaning of the word\n\nVilajnamanaya-- by a graceful person; Yasya- whose; Sthathum- to remain; Iksha-path- in front; Amuya- Shramika power\nBy; Vimohitah- those who are fascinated; Vikatthan- those who lament; Mama- this is mine; Aham- I am everything; Iti- in this way\nSaying good or bad; Durthiyah- in this way, bad thought was given.\nThe illusionary power (Maya) of God, being ashamed of its own position, cannot stand before it, but those who are fascinated by it, they, because of being absorbed in the thoughts of \"This is me\" and \"This is mine\", talk meaninglessly. Meaning: If the invincible, powerful, deceptive power of God, or the third power, which represents ignorance,\ncan enchant the entire world, even then it is not so strong that it can stand before God. Ignorance follows God and misleads the beings from there. Mohabroto.\nThe main characteristic of a living being is that it utters useless nonsense. It is not supported by the fag of Vedic literature\nAnd is the most inferior nonsense--''This is me, this is my God.\n\"Without God,\ncivilization runs on such false ideas, and such people, without the real experience of this,\nbelieve in false gods or those people, who are already deluded by the power of deception, to mislead,\ndeclare themselves as God. But those who live before God and those who\ntake refuge in Him are not influenced by the power of deception. Therefore, they remain free from this false notion