          "textEn": "27\nIt is extremely difficult to understand how the entire creation depends on the expansion of God's power, but\nGod has given a very beautiful example in the Bhagavad Gita. It is said in that, although air and\natoms are situated in the vast expanse of the sky, which is the abode of rest for every physical object,\neven then this sky remains separate and unaffected. Similarly, although God sustains every object produced by His power,\nHe remains separate. This has been accepted even by Shankaracharya, a strong supporter of the formless Brahman. They say Narayan: Parod Vyaktat, meaning Narayan,\nexists separate from his unique creative power. In this way, at the time of destruction, all this creation\nmerges within the divine body of Narayan, and this creation, again, from the same\nunchanging categories of fate and nature, emerges from their body.\nAll beings are described as being parts of God,\nbecause sometimes they are described as the soul--which is one of the spiritual structures. Because such\nliving beings, with complete attachment to the physical creation, keep being attracted, therefore they are different from God\nare. Kalad guna-vyatikar: Parinam swabhavat. Karma is the great cause of being born as a human being. 22). Meaning of the word\nFrom time--from eternity; Gunavyatikarah--change of qualities through reaction; Parinamah--change; Swabhavatah--from nature;\nKarmanah--from actions; Janma Srishti--creation of birth; Mahat--of great element; Purusha-adhisthitat--because of the incarnation of the Supreme Personality of Godhead; Abhut--from the first person incarnation (the preserver of the universe) of the Lord;\nAfter the incarnation of the great element or the physical creation (the preserver of the universe) of the first person, the principles of the great element or the physical creation\nare manifested, then time appears, and time--\nIn order, the three qualities appear. Nature means three qualitative expressions, which in actions\nare transformed.\nMeaning: By the omnipotence of God, the entire physical creation develops, transforms, and\n\nReactions occur through a sequential method, and by this omnipotence, they are sequentially gathered and\nremain protected in the body of God. Time is synonymous with nature and the physical creation"
