          "textEn": "224\n\nThose who, having believed thus, worship the enlightened ones. All the qualities of sensory perception come fully into the earth, and they, to some extent, manifest in other\nelements. In the sky, there is only sound, but in the air, there is both sound and touch. In fire, there are sound, touch, and shape, and in water, there are other sensations such as sound, touch, and shape.\nIn addition to these, there is also taste. But in the earth, in addition to the aforementioned qualities, there is also an additional development of smell. Therefore, there is a complete display of the diversity of life on Earth, that life which\noriginally starts by considering air as the basic element. Physical diseases occur within the physical body of living beings due to disturbances in the air.\nMental diseases occur within the body due to the special aggravation of air.\nTherefore, yogic exercises are especially beneficial in keeping the air in good condition, and with such exercises, the diseases of the body\nare almost negligible.\nBy doing yoga asanas properly, age also increases, and with such\nexercises, death can also be controlled. A complete yogi can dominate even death.\nAnd can leave the body at the right time, but only when he is able to take himself to the appropriate world. But devotion is greater than all yogis because it sends one beyond the material sky with its devotion-\nfilled service, and by the supreme will of the Lord, the controller of all,\nit is placed in any of the realms of Vaikuntha.\nVaikarikanmano janne deva vaikarika dasha.\nDigvatar-pracheto 5shvi-vahlindropeendro-mitra-kaha. 20>. Meaning of the word:\n\nFrom the Vaikarika Satoguna; Manah—mind; Jajne—wife; Devah—gods; Vaikarikah—in the Satoguna; Dashah—ten; Dik—the directions; Adhisthata—president; Vata—the presiding wind; Akam—the sun; Prachetah—Varuna; Ashwi—the son of Ashwini; Vahi—the fire god; Agni Deva—the king of Indra's heaven; Upendra—the god of heaven; Shri Vigraha—the form of Shri; Mitra—one of the twelve Adityas; Kaah—Prajapati Brahma..\n\nFrom the Satoguna, the mind is produced and manifested, along with the ten deities that control physical movements. Such a deity, controller of directions, controller of air, Suryadev, Daksha,\nPrajapati's father, Ashchinikumar, Agnidev, king of heaven (Indra), the venerable of heaven,\nArchavigraha, the chief of Adityas, and Prajapati Brahmaji are called. All exist in this way"
