          "textEn": "253\nThey are more in number than the souls who reside, and they alone, in the matter of immortality, fearlessness, and liberation from old age and disease,\nunderstand the importance of the aforementioned Sanjnini of God, Savit and Fie powers. In the physical world, all the realms are arranged in three spheres, called Triloka. These are\nHeaven, Earth, and the Nether Regions. All of this together is equal to one-fourth of the total power of God's treaty. Beyond this is the spiritual sky, which contains the Vaikuntha realm, beyond the seven layers of existence. In any of the three worlds, the state of immortality, complete knowledge, and complete bliss cannot be experienced.\nIt cannot be known. The three upper realms are called the Sattvic realms, because they provide relevant facilities of longevity, old age, and freedom from disease,\nand fearlessness.\nGreat sages and saints, beyond the heavens,\nreach the Maharloka, but this is also not a place of complete fearlessness, because at the end of an eon,\nthe Maharloka is destroyed, and its inhabitants have to be transferred to higher realms. Even in these worlds, liberation from death is not possible. Even though in these, the expansion of life, knowledge, and\njoy is more than expected, but true immortality, fearlessness, and freedom from old age and disease\nis only possible beyond the seven layers. Such things are situated in the head (Adhayi gg).\nThose who are surrounded by many weapons, those who are in the abode of many creatures,\nAnd those who are in the inner worlds, and those who are in the houses of the wise, and those who are in the Brihatlata. 20>. Meaning of the word:\n\nPada: three; Jagat: the world; Bahi: outside; Cha: and; Asan: were;\nAprajanam: those who are not reborn; Ye: those who; Ashramah: levels of life; Antarah: within; Trilokyah: of the three worlds;\nTu: but; Aparah: other; Griha-medhah: attached to household life; Avruhat: without observing the strict celibacy vow.