er scholar than Brahmaji, a Vedanti? But they admit that\neven after having complete knowledge of the Vedas, they are incapable of understanding the glories of God. Since there can be no one greater than Brahma,\ntherefore, how can the so-called Vedanti know about the ultimate truth?"
