 हमें भगवान्‌ के चरणकमलं में आत्म-समर्पण करना ही चाहिए । ब्रह्माजी पितामह कहलाते हैं,",
          "textEn": "272\nTherefore, without being trained in Vedanta (Bhakti-kādē) with the so-called Vedanti devotion, one cannot enter into the existence of God. The meaning of Vedanta is self-realization, and the meaning of devotion is to some extent the realization of God. No one can fully know God, but through self-dedication and\ndevotion, some things can be known, not by any other means. In the Brahma-Samhita also,\nIt is said-- Vedeshu durlabham, meaning that perhaps the existence of God can be known through the study of Vedanta,\nbut God is rare, yet easily accessible to his devotees. Therefore, Srila\nVyasadeva was not satisfied with the compilation of the Vedanta Sutras. After this, he compiled the Srimad Bhagavatam from the teachings of his guru Narada, so that the true essence of Vedanta can be understood.\nI am not that, I am the feet of those who are together.\nBhavachidam Swastyayanam Gage.\nHe who is the illusion of the self, I am the expansion,\nAs the sky is the end, where else is it? 26). Meaning of the word\nNa-Namaskar (Greetings); Asmi-I am; Aham-In me; Tat-Of that God; Charanam-On the feet; Samiyusham-Of the seeker;\nBhavat-Chidam-One who stops the cycle of birth and death; Swasti-Ayanam-Feeling of all happiness; Su-Mangalam-Auspicious\nBeneficial; Yah-Who; Hi-Indeed; Atma-Maya-Individual power; Vibhavam-Power; Sm-Indeed; Paryagat-Supposedly; Nishchay-Certainly; Atma-Antam-End of oneself; Ath-Therefore; Apar-Other; Kut-How\nHow.Therefore, it would be more beneficial for me to surrender myself at his feet, because\nOnly he can liberate a person from the cycle of birth and death. Such self-surrender is beneficial.\nOh, and from this, one experiences all happiness. Even the sky cannot fathom the limits of its expanse.\nTherefore, when God himself is unable to estimate his own limitations,\nthen what can others do? Meaning: The most learned among living beings, the supreme sacrificer, the supreme ascetic, and the supreme realized being,\nYogi Br