          "textEn": "280\nTherefore, this Mahavishnu is the first incarnation of this creation, and from him, the entire universe is created, and\none by one, all physical manifestations are created. The origin of the universe is done by God as a great\nelement, which exists in the spiritual sky as a cloud and is only a part of their various\nexpressions. The spiritual sky is the expansion of their individual rays.\nAnd they are also great elements, clouds. They lie down and create universes from their breath, and\nthen, as Garbhodakshayi Vishnu, entering each universe, they create Brahma, Shiva, and\nother numerous gods for its sustenance, and in the end, they incorporate all of them into their bodies,\nas is confirmed in the Bhagavad Gita (9.7)--\n\nTHAI Kaunteya gid yanti phh |\n\nAt the end of the eon, I will be born again. YR Kuntiputra! When the Kalpa, that is, the age of Brahma, ends, all the created manifestations\nMy nature, that is, enters into power, and when I desire again, then again that same creation of mine\nemerges from self-power.The conclusion is that all this is merely a display of the inconceivable powers of God, about which\nno one can have complete information. We have said this before as well. Pure, only, knowledge, self-existent, perfectly situated.\n\nTruth, complete, beginning, endless, without attributes, eternal, non-dual. 40>. The sages, having heard this, were filled with wonder.\n"
