          "textEn": "283\nWorkers desire the reward for their actions, yogis desire some kind of accomplishment in life, and the knowledgeable seek to be absorbed in the existence of God. But as long as the demand for sensual pleasure remains,\nthere is no opportunity to be at peace. On the contrary, unnecessary dry arguments spoil the whole matter, and in this way, God also moves further away from our understanding. But by continuing to follow the principles of dry\nthought, one can know the unparalleled form of God to some extent, yet they cannot understand His supreme Govinda form, because those who are completely\nsinless or immaculate, they alone accept the pure devotion of God, whose confirmation\nhas been given in the Bhagavad Gita (7.28):\n\nThose who are purified by the merit of their actions,\nthey are liberated by the merit of their actions. The first incarnation is the Supreme Being.\nTime is the nature, and the self is the mind.\nMatter, form, quality, senses,\nThe cosmic, the self-existent, the unmoving, the moving, the earth. 42). Shabdartham\nAadi: Pratham; Avatarah-- Avatar; Purushah-- Purusha, the cause, the reservoir of Vishnu; Parasya-- of the Lord; Kaalah-- time, the measure; Swabhaavah-- nature; Sat-phalaah-- the fruit of nature; Asat-- the cause; Manah-- mind; Cha-- also; Dravyam-- substance; Vikarah-- the material ego; Gunah--\nQualities of nature; Indriyan-- senses; Virat— got body; Swarat-- the womb-dwelling Vishnu; Sthasnu-- unmoving; Charishnu-- moving;\nBhumna-- of the Lord.. He is eternal, time, sky, action-\ncause, mind, elements, physical ego, qualities of nature, senses, the immense form of God,\nGarbhodakshayi Vishnu and the lord of all moving and non-moving beings. Meaning: We have explained many times before that this physical creation is not permanent. This is merely a temporary display of the material power of the Almighty God.\nThis physical creation is necessary to provide opportunities for those bound souls\nwho are not willing to form a relationship with God through divine love and devotion. Such bound souls were not allowed to enter the liberated life of the divine realm"
