          "textEn": "298\nVanaprastha and Sanyas. In the first stage of life, which lasts for the first twenty-five years, a person should be\neducated as a celibate under the guidance of an authentic guru, so that he can understand\nthat woman is the real binding power of this world. If someone wants freedom from the bonds of a bound life,\nthen he should be free from the attraction of women. For souls, woman is the enchanting element,\nBut in human form, especially in human life, it is for self-realization. The whole world is driven by the magic of woman's\nattraction, and man is not connected to the rope that he gets caught in the hard knot of worldly bondage.\nHe gets trapped.\nUpon becoming associated with a woman, under the intoxication of false prestige of ownership, the desire to assert one's dominance over the material\nworld arises. <silence_gap> | To obtain a house, land, and children, to become important in society, love for caste and birthplace, greed for wealth, all these are like a web of illusion or\nlike a dream, they surround man, and man forgets the true purpose of his life,\nand his progress in the direction of self-realization is obstructed. A bachelor is usually of a higher caste,\nthat is, a boy of the Brahmin, Kshatriya, or Vaishya caste. Under the guidance of an authentic guru, he receives education from the age of five\nto the age of twenty-five, and experiences gaining specific education for the values of life and\nfor livelihood. Thereafter, the bachelor is allowed to go home,\nwhere he marries a suitable woman to enter married life.\nBut there are many celibates who do not go home to become householders, but they live a life of a devoted celibate without any kind of contact with women. They accept the monastic order. They know very well that the company of a woman is a hindrance, which hinders self-realization.\nIt creates obstacles. Because in special age, the desire for sexual pleasure becomes extremely strong, therefore the Guru can allow a celibate to\nmarry; this exemption is only given to those who cannot remain a lifelong celibate. And such discrimination is only possible for an authentic Guru, thus a so-called family planning program is necessary. The householder who, after proper education in celibacy, follows the scripturally approved method\nof Hoff, is not like a householder who is like a dog and a cat. Such a householder fifty"
