          "textEn": "33\nThe maternal heart saw all the universes present within him. He was very surprised, but he\nthought that the almighty Narayan had done this to protect his son from all kinds of dangers\nby keeping watch. Because of the deep love for Krishna, she could never even imagine\nthat her son is none other than Lord Narayan himself. This is the inner power of God, Yogamaya, in which\nthe pastimes of God are completed with various types of devotees. Without God, such strange games,\nWho can play? One who is free from fear, is freed from the noose of Varuna.\nOne who is hidden in the cowsheds, is freed from the noose of Maya.\nHaving been created, he sleeps all night, in great restlessness.\nHe places the world in a state of weakness, like Gokul. 29). Meaning of the word\n\nNandam- to Nand (Krishna's religious father); Cha-- also; Mokshyati-- saves; Bhayat-- from fear; Varunasya- of the god Varuna of water;\nPashat- from the noose; Gopan- to the cowherds; Bileshu- in the mountain cave; Pihitan- kept; Mayasununa- by the son of Maya; Cha-\nalso; Adhi- from the daytime; Vyaktam- busy; Nishchitam- definitely;\nLokam- world; Vikuntham- Vaikuntha; Upaneshyati- is given; Gokulam- the supreme world; Sm- certainly;\nNishchitam- definitely;\nBhagavan- Lord; Vaikuntha- Vaikuntha; Govinda- the son of Govardhana; Govinda- the son of Govardhana; Govinda- the son of Govardhana; Govind Lord Krishna saved his father Nanda Maharaj from the fear of Varuna and freed the cowherds\nfrom the cave of the mountain, where the son of Maya had imprisoned them. Not only this,\nLord Shri Krishna made all the residents of Vrindavan, who, being busy with work all day and sleeping peacefully at night,\nbecame a part of the supreme abode in the afterlife.\nAll these works are divine.\nAnd they are the ones who prove their divinity. Meaning: Once, due to a misunderstanding, in the middle of the night, Shri Krishna's religious father, Nand Maharaj, thinking that\nthe night has ended, wen