गवान्‌ द्वारा या उनके पार्षदों द्वारा मारे जाएंगे | इन सबका स्पष्ट वर्णन दशम why में किया\nजाएगा। किन्तु हमें ज्ञात होना चाहिए कि उपर्युक्त सभी जीवात्माएँ या तो ब्रह्म-ज्योति में मिल करके या\nभगवान्‌ के धाम वैकुण्ठ लोक में प्रविष्ट होकर मोक्ष प्राप्त करेंगी । इसकी व्याख्या भीष्मदेव द्वारा पहले\nही (प्रथम why में) हो चुकी है। जिन व्यक्तियों ने कुरुक्षेत्र की युद्धभूमि में या अन्यत्र भगवान्‌ या\nबलदेव इत्यादि के साथ युद्ध किया है, वे मृत्यु के समय अपनी मानसिक अवस्था के अनुसार\nआध्यात्मिक पद प्राप्त करेंगे। जो ईश्वर को पहचान गए थे वे वैकुण्ठ में प्रविष्ट होगे ओर जिन्होंने ईश्वर\nको परमशक्तिमान रूप में अनुभव किया है वे ब्रह्मज्योति में विलीन होकर मोक्ष प्राप्त करेगे | लेकिन\nउनमें से सभी भौतिक संसार से मुक्त हो जाएँगे। जब भगवान्‌ के साथ शत्रुता रखने का ऐसा लाभ",
          "textEn": "335\nThese all; Ch-completely; Pralamba- named demon; Khar- named demon; Dadur- named demon; Keshi- named demon;\nArishta- named demon; Malla- wrestler of Kansa's court; Ibh- named demon; Kuvalayapida; Kansa- king of Mathura and Shri Krishna's\nMaternal uncle; Yavanas- kings of Persia and other neighboring countries; Kapi- Dvivida; Paundraka- Ayadya: --Paundraka etc.; others--others;\nCh--also; Shalva--King Shalva; Kuja--Narakasura; Bala--King Bala; Danvakra--the dead infant Shishupala's brother, Of Krishna\nAdversary; Saptoksha- King Saptoksha; Shambara-- King Shambara; Viduratha-- King Viduratha; Rukmi- Chief; Rukmini's brother; Ye- These all; Va- Or; Mrideh- In the battlefield; Samiti- Shalin- Extremely powerful; Atta- Chapa-\nArmed with bow and arrow; Kamboj- King of Kamboj; Matsya- King of Matsya; Kuru- Son of Dhritarashtra; Srujjaya- King Srujjaya;\nKaikaya- Originally; King of Kaikaya and others; Yasyanti- Will obtain; Adarshanam- Unparalleled meeting from Brahmajyoti; Alam- What\nSay, the strength-- Baladeva, the foremost of the Krishnas; Partha-- Arjuna; Bhima-- Bhima, the second among the Pandavas; Vyaja-Ahayena-- by the six names;\nHarina-- by Hari; Nilayam-- abode; Tadiyam-- his \\. Pralamba, Dhenuka, Bak, Keshi, Arishta, Chanura, Mushtik, Kubalayapida elephant, Kansa, Yavana,\nAsuras like Narakasura, Shalva, Dwivida, Vanara and Bavala, Dantavakra, Satasad,\nShambara, Viduratha and Rukmi like Sipahsalar and Kamboj, Matsya, Kuru, Srunjaya and Kekaya\nLike brave warriors, directly from Hari or Baldev, Arjun, Under the guise of names like Bhima,\nthey themselves will engage in a fierce battle with Shri Bhagavan, and all the demons killed in this way will either attain Nirvisha\nBrahmajyoti or attain the abode of Lord located in Vaikuntha Loka.\n\nMeaning: In both the physical and spiritual worlds, all the incarnations that occur are a display of the various powers of Lord Krishna. Baldev is the closest relative of Shri Bhagwan, but Arjun,\nBheem is his personal attendant.\nWhen God appears with all his councilors and powers (or\nwhen they appear, in the same way) then mischievous people and demons like Pralamba, or Asuri people, either\nwill be killed by God himself or by his councilors. A clear description of all this will be given in Dasham Why. But we should know that all the above souls, either by merging into the Brahma-Jyoti or\nby entering the abode of God, Vaikuntha Loka, will attain salvation. Its interpretation has already been done by Bhishmadeva in the first\n(first why). Those individuals who have fought in the battlefield of Kurukshetra or elsewhere with God or\nBaldev etc., at the time of death, according to their mental state,\nwill attain spiritual status. Those who had recognized God will enter Vaikuntha, and those who have experienced God\nas the supreme power will merge into Brahmajyoti and attain salvation. But\nall of them will be freed from the material world.\nWhen there is such a benefit of having enmity with God"
