          "textEn": "339\nare considered equivalent to ornaments, and when such floods of ornaments come in society, then\nmany inequalities arise in the progressive, peaceful life of man. In the upper classes of society,\ndue to lack of training or culture, they are no longer entitled to be called 'Dwija-Jan'. The importance of 'Dwija'\nis explained in these great texts in many places, but it is again worth mentioning here\nthat the birth resulting from the union of parents is called animal birth. But such animal birth and\ndiet, sleep, fear, sexuality based animal life is a scientific culture of spiritual life\nwithout Shudra life, that is, the uncultured life of lower class people. It is mentioned here that\nin Kali Yuga, the administrative power of society will go into the hands of the uncultured, devoid of God, laboring class.\nAnd the Nrudeva (or government HATO) will be Vrushal, meaning the lower uncultured people of society.\nIf human\nsociety remains filled with uncultured, lower-class people, then the hope of happiness and peace is futile. In humans, such uncivilized social animals have characteristics already present. It is the duty of the public leaders to pay attention to this\nAnd to try to improve the social system by establishing trained Brahmins in the knowledge of the essence. This is possible only through the spread of the culture of Shri Padbhagwat in the whole world. Man\nWhen society declines, God appears as Kalki Avatar and, being merciless,\nkills all the demonic people.\nI am the one who performs penance, the nine ascetics,\nAnd the ones who are in the place, the Dharma-Makha-Manvamravanisha.\nAt the end, the ones who are the destroyers of unrighteousness, the Munyas, the Vasasuras, and others,\nThe ones who are the manifestations of Maya, the power of the Supreme Being. 39). Meaning of the word:\nSage - At the beginning of creation; Tapah - Penance; Aham - In; Rishayah - Sages; Navah - Nine; Ye Prajesah - Those who are the creators;\nSthana