          "textEn": "362\nThrough self-realization, he immediately becomes a part of God's divine love and devotion. ©. All like Narad,\npure devotees were not only self-realized beings, but they were engaged in the work of giving advice for their own happiness.\nAnd in this way, they liberated many inferior beings trapped in the qualities of Maya. They were so powerful\nThat it was possible, because they regularly listened to and worshiped the principles of the Bhagavata. The accumulated material desires get purified by the Lord through his own efforts, through such actions. God is always present in the hearts of living beings, but He manifests through devotional service. The purification of the heart through the practice of knowledge or yoga can be suitable for a person for some time.\nBut it is like purifying a small amount of still water with chemical methods.\nIn this way, the water is purified, and due to the silt settling for some time,\nit can remain clean, but it becomes dirty again if shaken even slightly. The point is that\ndevotion to God and service is the only way to keep the heart clean forever. Other\nMethods may be superior for some time, but there is a fear of becoming confused again due to the disturbance of the mind. The best method to get rid of the clutches of Maya is to listen to Shrimad Shagavat regularly with devotion. The self-controlled man does not abandon the root of Krishna's feet.\nThe liberated one, having experienced the suffering of his own self, takes refuge in his own self. 6. Meaning of the word:\nDhaut-Atma--those whose hearts have become pure; Purushah--the living being; Krishna Shri Bhagavant's; Pada-Mulam--the refuge of the lotus feet;\nNa- not; Majhamti--leaves; Mukta Mukta; Sarva- all; Parikleshah--of all the sufferings of life; Pandhah--traveler; Swa-\nSharanam--to one's abode; Yatha- as.\n.\nA pure devotee of God, whose heart has once been purified by devotion, he\nnever abandons the lotus feet of Shri Krishna, because God gives him the same supreme\nsatisfaction as a traveler receives in his home after a difficult journey.\nMeaning: One who is not a pure devotee of Lord Krishna, his heart is not completely clean, but\na person with a completely pure heart never abandons the devotion to God. Brahmaji told Narada"
