          "textEn": "372\nMeaning of the word\nYugani- different eras; Yugamanam-- the duration of each era; Ch-- also; Dharma-- specific actions; Yah Ch-- and who; Yuge Yuge--\nIn each era; Avatar-- incarnation; Anucharitam-- and the actions of the incarnation; Yat- that; Aashcharyam- most wonderful;\nHareh Parameshwar HTL\nPlease describe the different eras of creation and the periods of all of them. Tell me about the various incarnations of God in different eras. Meaning: Lord Shri Krishna is the first Lord, and all the incarnations of God are inseparable from Him.\nEven being, they originate from Him. Maharaj Parikshit asked the supreme scholar and great sage Shukdev Goswami about\nthe activities of such incarnations, so that the incarnation of God could be confirmed in authentic scriptures\nbased on the activities mentioned in them.\nMaharaj Parikshit, a common man,\nwas not one to easily accept the incarnation of God by being swept away in thought, but he\nwanted to accept it only on the basis of the described in Vedic literature and the confirmed characteristics by the Acharyas like Srila Shukadeva Goswami. God descends from his inner power, without any\nnecessity of natural laws; as a result, his actions are also unusual. Of God\nSpecific activities are mentioned and we have to know that the activities of God and himself\nGod is one because he is situated at the highest level. Therefore, to listen about the activities of God,\nmeans to have direct association with God, and the direct association of God means, oh, from the material impurities,\npurification. We have already discussed this in the previous section.\nThe ordinary dharma of men is also special, and so is that.\nThe dharma of the best of men, the kingly, and the wretched is to live in distress. 18. Shabdartham\nNrnam- of human society; sarvam- common; dharmah- religious contact; sutra; sa- special; vi- specific; cha- also; yahshah- they;\nIn the manner that; grenaam- of the three varnas; rajarshii