          "textEn": "379\nAs the self-possessed one, the Lord, is deluded by the self-possessed Maya,\nHe, abandoning that delusion, is directly the all-pervading Lord. 23). Meaning of the word\nYatha-- as; Atma-tanrah-- self-controlled; Bhagavan-- Lord; Vikridati-- performs Leela (divine play); Atma-mayaya-- with one's own sam\nPower; Visujya-- renouncing; Va-- also; Yatha-- as; Mayamu-- external power; Udaste-- remains;\nSakshivat- like a witness; Vibhuh-- almighty..\nThe independent God, with his inner power, enjoys his pastimes, and at the time of dissolution,\nHe bestows them upon the external power and remains as a witness himself.\nMeaning: Lord Krishna, being the complete Supreme Personality of Godhead, and the reason for the destruction of all other incarnations,\nHe alone is the only independent person. He enjoys the pastimes through creation according to His will,\nand at the time of dissolution, He bestows the external power upon them. Only through the internal power, He kills Putana,\nthough He performs pastimes in the lap of Mother Yashoda. When they want to depart from this world,\nthey create a play of destroying their own lineage (Yadu-Kul), and remain unaffected by such destruction. Those who are witnessing whatever is happening, even then they have nothing to do with it. They are all independent in every way. A pure devotee should know all this well, that is why\nMaharaj Parikshit, to know completely, expressed curiosity.\nI ask the Lord of all, beginning with 'anu' and 'purva'.\nHe should explain the secret of that in detail to the one who has surrendered. 24). Meaning of the word\nSarvam- all; Etat- this; Cha-- because of not being able to ask; Bhagavan- O sage; Prichchhata- of the inquisitive; Me- in me;\nAnuprvarshah- from the beginning; Tattvatah- in essence -According to truth; Arhasi-- Please tell; Udaharitum-- As you will tell; Prapannaya--\nSurrounded; Maha-Mune-- O sage.\nO Maharishi, as the representative of God, please pacify my curiosity regarding all those inquiries about which\nI have asked you questions and also about those in whose inquiries I have not been able to present from the beginning of my inquiry,\nplease pacify my curiosity. Since I have come to your refuge,\ntherefore, grant me complete knowledge in this matter."
