          "textEn": "396\n\nWhen Brahmaji was not understanding how the creation of the universe should be done, then he\nwent inside the water to find out the source of the lotus-seat and the means of creation, where he\nheard the sound of the word 'Tap' twice. To accept the path of penance is like a second birth for the seeker. Here,\nthe word 'Upashrayan' is very meaningful. It is like Upanayan, that is, like bringing a disciple close to the guru on the path of penance. Therefore, Brahmaji was initiated by Shri Krishna, and this was confirmed by Brahmaji himself.\nIn his work, Brahma-Samhita, it is said. In the Brahma-Samhita, in each verse, Brahmaji has worshiped Govinda and other great beings.\nI am praising you. In this way, Shri Krishna initiated Brahma through the Krishna Mahamantra, so that before creating the vast\nuniverse, he could become a Vaishnava, that is, a devotee of God. It is mentioned in the Brahma-Samhita\nthat Brahmaji was initiated into the eighteen-letter Krishna mantra, which is generally accepted by all devotees of Krishna.\nWe follow the same principle, because we have a connection with the Brahma Sampradaya,\nwhich is directly from Brahma to Narad, from Narad to Vyas, from Vyas to Madhvamuni, from Madhvamuni to wees Puri, and from Madhavendra\nPuri to Ishwar Puri, from Ishwar Puri to Bhagavan Chaitanya, and respectively our Guru Bhagavatkripamurti Bhaktisiddhanta\nis in the Saraswati Kaushishi disciple lineage. In this way, the person who is initiated into the disciple-lineage receives the same fruit or the power to create.\nHe receives it. For a devotee without auspiciousness, chanting this sacred mantra is the only refuge. Only\nthrough such penance, a devotee of God attains all accomplishments like Brahmaji.\nWithout moving, he looked with unwavering gaze.\nHe saw something else there, unseen.\nHaving rested in his own self, he pondered over that.\nHe meditated on what was prescribed by the ascetics. 7/. Meaning of the word\n\nNishamy