          "textEn": "397\nBut when they could not find anyone extra to themselves, they considered it better to sit hastily on a lotus seat\nand pay attention to doing penance as per the order.\n\nMeaning: To achieve success in life, one should follow the example of Brahmaji,\nbecause he is the original creature of creation. Upon being initiated into penance by God, he resolved to perform penance,\nand upon finding no one around him except himself, he could understand\nthat the sound was made by God himself. At that time, Brahma was completely alone, because at that time there was no creation,\nand there was no one else there besides him. In the first chapter of the first Why of Shrimad Bhagwat,\nin the first verse, Shri Bhagwan initiated Brahma from within his heart. God is within each\nsoul, situated as the Supreme Soul, and he initiated Brahma because he\nwas eager to take initiation.\nSimilarly, whoever is willing to take initiation, God can give initiation to him. As it has been told, Brahma is the original guru of this universe, and since God himself had initiated him,\ntherefore, the story of Shrimad Bhagwat has been going on through the disciple tradition, that is why to get the real story (message) of Shrimad Bhagwat,\na person should go to the guru who has been going on through the disciple tradition. Then, in that tradition, after being initiated by a worthy guru, one should engage in penance to worship him.\nOne should become absorbed in it. But considering himself equal to Brahma, one should not think of being initiated directly by God,\nbecause in this era, no person can be considered pure equal to Brahma. For the creation of the universe, the burden of Brahma's position is entrusted to the most pure being,\nand until he is equally worthy, he cannot be considered equal to Brahma.\nBut he can get the same facilities by the pure devotees of God, by the orders of the scriptures (as especially in Bhagavad Gita and Srimad Bhagavatam) and by an authentic guru. The man who\nis devoted to the service of God from the heart, before him God himself appears in the form of a guru. Therefore, that authentic guru, who by fate attains a devoted disciple, is the greatest of God's"
